1265	Immutability means God is unchanging in his being, perfections, purposes and promises. God id essentially immutable and relationally mutable. The biblical concept of immutability does not mean that God is inactive, but constantly interacting with his creation in real and meaningful ways. According to traditional Christian theology, there are three critical aspects of immutability.\n1. God's eternal counsel or ultimate plan for history is immutable. Different traditions understand God's eternal plan differently, but all agree that all that God has done, doing and will do are part of a unified plan. God uses his omniscience to direct history towards the ends for which he created it. The immutability of God's plan assures us that His will and ways in ancient times accord with his will and ways today. \n2. God is immutable in his character. God's eternal nature is the same even though he displays different aspects of his nature in different times. This helps us to see that there will be significant connections between the original meaning and modern applications of the scripture. A particular attribute in a passage is understood in the context of God's other attributes. Some way modern audience are expected to apply the emphases of every scripture in ways that never disregard any other attribute of God. \n3. Covenant promises. When God promises, his word is immutable. God made covenant with Abraham and it remained for ever. If it is not covenant, God changes mind. Eg. His word about the destruction of Nineveh. Every revelation of God in scripture assures that God will keep his covenant promises. The original audience were supposed to understand every passage of scripture in this light, and modern audience should do the same	8	2019-10-22 15:16:03+05:30	2019-10-22 19:11:49+05:30	\N	331	692
1266	There are at least three ways in which modern people are very similar to the people who first received the scripture. \n1. Sinful images: Human beings created in the image of God, have fallen in to sin. All human despite of period, color or language have totally deprived from God and have a fallen, sinful nature. All human beings are marred in the image of God due to fall. \n2. Religious divisions: Since the beginning, the readers of the scriptures fallen in to one of three religious groups: unbelievers, false believers and believers. Unbelievers refuse to submit to God, false believers make superficial commitments to God but not truly redeemed. Believers are people who make faithful commitments to God, redeemed from sin and saved from eternal judgement.\nJust as in the past modern applications calls unbelievers to repentance exposing their lost condition. For false believers scripture expose their hypocrisies  and call for repentance. For believers biblical texts were designed to restrain their sin, to warn against failure and to lead them to grateful living. \n3. Classes; People are classified on the basis of gender, age, wealth, profession etc. The Bible also speak of people classified on the basis of their background. The same classes of people exist in every age. This forms meaningful connections between the original audience and all subsequent audiences.	8	2019-10-22 15:30:23+05:30	2019-10-22 19:11:49+05:30	\N	331	693
