1310	The term New covenant is derived from Jeremiah 31:31 where the prophet predicted that God would grant a covenant of final renewal to Israel and Judah. In eight ways this covenant is described in Hebrews. \n1. Hebrews 8:1-13 introduces the idea that Jesus mediates the New covenant as the Royal high priest in heaven. The Levitical priesthood failed to accomplish the purpose but the New covenant is based on a better promise through Christ. 8:6\n2. Jesus' heavenly priesthood is superior to the Levitical priesthood. Sacrifices of the earthly tabernacle could not fully resolve the problem of sin but had to be repeated. But Jesu did away with sin once for all because his blood is sprinkled in man made sanctuary. \n3. Hebrews 10:1-18 compare and contrast the Old and New covenants and declare that the animal sacrifices needed because Jesus brought final forgiveness of sin through his sacrifice. \n4. Jesus has opened the way in to the most holy place. Hebrews 10:19-23\n5. There is severity of punishment upon them that deny the salvation through Christ. Hebrews 10:24-31.\n6. The audience are exhorted not to throw away their confidence through Christ. !0;32-35.\n7. Hebrews 10:36-39 warns that God does not take pleasure in those who withdraw from living by faith. \n8. Hebrews 11 gives a long list of saints and explained, they would share with the audience in being made perfect when Christ returns. \nBy all these references and explanations the author established the superiority of the New Covenant in Christ.	9	2020-02-21 15:38:32+05:30	2020-02-22 05:23:37+05:30	\N	388	783
