1324	There is a sound theological basis for emphasizing three aspects of original meaning in our investigation of Scripture. They are 1. writer 2. audience . document. \nWRITER- The HOly Spirit chose to communicate through the personalities , experiences,emotions and patterns of thought of human biblical writers.  \n AUDIENCE- God always accommodated his revelation to his original audiences so that they could understand .Divine accommodation is the idea that God designed his revelation to be understood by its first audience.\nDOCUMENT-The theological basis for emphasizing the biblical documents can be found in two important doctrines : the doctrine of organic inspiration and doctrine of divine accommodation. The doctrine of divine inspiration teaches that Holy Spirit inspired human authors to write scripture. The doctrine of divine accommodation implies that everything in Scripture  like its words ,grammar and literary style rose out of the cultural and linguistic conventions of its day	8	2020-03-26 06:18:35+05:30	2020-03-27 09:25:25+05:30	\N	395	681
1325	ORGANIC INSPIRATION teaches that Holy Spirit inspired human authors to write Scripture. But it doesn't not say that every copy made of that document will be perfect or that every translation made from that document will be perfect.Because the doctrine of inspiration extends only to the original texts of Scripture , only those documents have the full authority of God himself. The Changes that have taken place in these texts as they have been copied over the centuries are not our inspired by God and neither are the translations too. so in order to increase our confidence that we have rightly understood the original meaning of the scripture , we should study the writings that God actually inspired.\nDIVINE ACCOMMODATION  : the  doctrine of accommodation implies that everything in scripture like its words , grammar and literary style rose out of the cultural and linguistic conventions of its day. So if we pay careful attention to the ways o Scripture reflects , we will more correctly understand it.	9	2020-03-26 06:30:01+05:30	2020-03-27 09:25:25+05:30	\N	395	682
1326	Having an access to many manuscripts that contain the the original words of Scripture  by the scholars helps us to understand the original meaning of the inspiration. Modern translations are not infallible , but they do  represent one of the most important teaching ministries of the church. In order to grasp the original meaning of Biblical passages access to original manuscripts is very important.  Modern Christians have the advantage of many decades of scholarly research devoted to studying and comparing ancient copies of scripture. These explorations are have confirmed over and over that the Hebrew and Greek texts if the Bible are far more reliable than the texts we have of most other ancient writings.	8	2020-03-26 06:47:45+05:30	2020-03-27 09:25:25+05:30	\N	395	683
1327	There afre three major appraches toward tge objects and subjects of knowledge . OBJECTIVISM , SUBJECTIVISM  AND DIALOGISM\nOBJECTIVE APPROACH says that under the right circumstances its possible to arrive at impartial or objective knowledge. They believe that this way they can interpret scripture impartially  and they can know its meaning with relative certainity.\nSUBJECTIVE APPROACH SAYS that our knowledge is always influenced by our personal biases, making impartial objectivity impossible. They recognize that human beings and the world , especially matters if faith are often too complex to be discerned by the scientific rationalism.\nDIALOGICAL APPRAOCH empasizes the constant dailog or interplay between the objective reality and our subjective perspectives. The word dialogical refers to the idea that interpratation involves atype of dilaog or discussion between the reader and the text.	9	2020-03-26 07:08:59+05:30	2020-03-27 09:25:25+05:30	\N	395	684
