1333	Biblical theology is in large measure a response to cultural shifts that can be traced back to the enlightenment of the 17th century. This is not to say that the concern of biblical theology were entirely new or belong only to the modern period, Christian have always explored the act of God reported in scripture but in the modern period significant cultural shifts took place that led theologians to emphasize these historical interests as never before. Many forms of historic-ism rose to prominence like archaeological discoveries, geology, biology in terms of Darwinian theory. Similarly also took place in theology. Therefore with the emphasis of modern historic ism , Christian Theologians also responded to theology in these ways.	8	2020-03-30 22:01:14+05:30	2020-03-31 05:54:17+05:30	\N	401	657
1335	Modern Historic ism inspired many critical theologians to approach the scripture with new questions and priorities. We can grasp the heart of the matter by briefly touching on two historical stages of development that the early stages in the 18th century and second of the later developments in recent history.\nJohann Gabbler spoke of dogmatic or systematic theology. The goal of systematic theology was not to examine or explain the Bible but to determine what Christians should believe in the modern world through science and religion. Instead of treating the Bible as true history they began to look at the scriptures as expressions of ancient religious sentiments presented as historical claims and they explored how these religious feelings and experiences might be useful to modern Christians.	7	2020-03-30 22:14:02+05:30	2020-03-31 05:54:17+05:30	\N	401	658
