1391	In Matthew 13-25, Jesus explained that the kingdom of God would come in three phases. It would begin with the first coming in a small way, Jesus' earthly ministry would inaugurate the age to come with some blessings and judgement of the last days. The second phase is the continuation. the age to come would continue alongside this age for a period of time as Christ reigned in heaven and his church grew. And then at the second coming of Christ the age to come would reach its consummation and this age of sin and death would come to an end. Jesus' teaching about the last days represented one of the most decisive ways in which Christians had broken with first century Judaism. Jewish religious leaders and General Jewish population raged against Christianity precisely because of the Christian outlook on the Messianic last days.  Christians believed that the Messiah had already come, but in a way that was unexpected. The new testament authors deeply preoccupied with Jesus' three phase eschatology and this preoccupation is reflected in everything they wrote.	7	2020-04-10 21:26:54+05:30	2020-04-10 21:50:18+05:30	\N	415	673
