1447	Our definition of Christian ethics focuses on God and His blessings rather than on terms like good or evil, or right or wrong. Those things that receive God's blessings are good and right, whereas those things that do not receive his blessing are wrong and evil.\n1.DIVINE NATURE- God himself is the ultimate standard of right and wrong,of good and evil.God is not accountable to any standard outside himself.\n2 DIVINE ACTIONS-God's actions demonstrates the standard of morality. God shows his approval by bestowing blessings. He shows his hatred by withholding blessings and pouring out curses. Many times the Bible communicates right and wrong by recording God's reactions rather that by explicitly labeling things good or evil.	7	2020-04-28 06:09:31+05:30	2020-04-30 01:14:11+05:30	\N	436	826
1448	Obedience to God's commands must be done with proper motive.Unless a work is done with right motive , it is not a work that God will reward with blessings. \n\n1.FAITH\nOnly believers who are indwelled by the Holy Spirit can do works that God rewards with blessings.\nOnly believers have hearts that are purified by faith. Saving faith motivates good works. This is the faith possessed by believers and only by believers. Unless our attempts to seeks God's blessings are founded on faith, we cannot please God and therefore cannot be rewarded by Him.\n2. LOVE\nOur works are useless if they are not motivated by love.\nWorks and even spiritual gifts that produce beneficial results merit no reward if they are not motivated by love.\nLove is an aspect of every law God requires us to obey . If we do not act in love, no work we do can conform to his standard.Our love mist be both for God and neighbor.	8	2020-04-28 06:20:51+05:30	2020-04-30 01:14:11+05:30	\N	436	827
1449	THREEFOLD CRITERIA\nWestminister Confession of faith says" Works done by ungenerate men may be things which God commands and of good use both to themselves and others , yet because they proceed not from an heart purified by faith, nor are done in a right manner , according to the word; nor to a right end , the glory of God;they are therefore sinful and cannot please God.\nThe threefold criteria are\n1.PROPER MOTIVE\nUnless a work is done with right motive , it is not a work that God will reward his blessings.Only believers are hearts are purified by faith. saving faith motivates good works. Our works are useless if they are not motivate by love Our love must be both for God and neighbor\n2. PROPER STANDARD\nIn order for works to be good , they must be done according to the standard of Word of God, God's revelation.All commands of scriptures are designed to guide us.\n3. PROPER GOAL\nGood works may have any number of innumerate goals. Everything in the Christian life should be done in a way that honors God and brings Him glory. God approves of works intended to bring him glory and He condemns works that disregard or oppose his glory	9	2020-04-28 06:35:18+05:30	2020-04-30 01:14:11+05:30	\N	436	828
1450	Ethical judgement involves the applications of God's Word to a situation by a person.\nEthics should be done from three perspectives:\n1.GOD'S WORD\n2.SITUATION\n3. PERSON\nThe best approach is to do ethics from all three perspectives and to let the insights from each perspective inform and influence the others\n1. SITUATIONAL\nProblems\nconsequences of actions\ngoals\nwhen our ethical inquiries turn to the problems themselves, or to the consequences of actions or to the goals.\n2.Normative- God's Word is the norm or standard for ethics . We are doing ethics from the normative perspective when we look to the Bible to tell us what to do\n\n3. Existential- When we approach ethics by asking questions that are specific to the people involved, we are doing ethics from an existential perspective	8	2020-04-28 06:45:33+05:30	2020-04-30 01:14:11+05:30	\N	436	829
