1452	Traditionally , theologians have spoken of God's revelation primarily in three categories :\n1. GENERAL REVELATION\nCreation and history teach us true things about God and his moral requirements. General revelation cannot teach us everything, but it speaks clearly enough to teach us true  things about God.\ncomplexity- some aspects of general revelation are common to all people ,but others are restricted to very limited groups of people. Scripture is the supreme form of revelation in our day , but we affirm the validity and binding authority of general revelation. .God 's revelation in creation and history is clear, but people reject it and convince themselves of falsehood\n2.SPECIAL REVELATION-\nIT is the norm that is binding in our lives. Most rely on the spoken word or written word ,but all involve GOd communicating with people in ways that transcend the normal workings of creation\nThe only universally acknowledged form of current special revelation is Scripture.The Bible is binding on all people at all times\n3.EXISTENTIAL REVELATION\nGOD uses councils, ancient writers, doctrines of men and private spirits to reveal his will to the people. The external aspects of existential revelation are human existence, human judgement both individual and corporate and human behavior \nThe internal aspects  is illumination of the Holy Spirit which is a divine gift of understanding that God gives to believers and even to unbelievers.	9	2020-04-28 07:12:30+05:30	2020-04-30 01:14:11+05:30	\N	436	831
