1475	The Bible is divinely inspired , so it carries God's authority.\n1. CLAIM OF AUTHORITY-\nIn the earliest history recorded in the Bible , God spoke directly to humanity and his speech carried authority. All things were created by the power of his word. In the days of Moses  ,God encoded his spoken word in the written form . His spoken word is the basis for his written word. God's written word is his authoritative covenant document that his people are obligated to obey. Jesus frequently appealed to scripture to justify and explain his actions. Paul believed that the scriptures are God's authoritative word and that they bind New Testament believers.\nIMPLICATIONS \nBecause Scriptures carries  God's authority, we are morally obligated to conform all our choices, actions thoughts and feelings to it. We must keep the breadth of Biblical instruction . We are not to obey what we like and to ignore what we don not like. We all fall into the trap of unconscious selectivity. We must constantly be remind of those commands which we may have forgotten or overlooked. Only when we embrace the Scripture from the heart can we rightly submit to the authority of God's word.	9	2020-05-02 06:15:43+05:30	2020-05-05 09:51:31+05:30	\N	439	834
