1513	God's plan to redeem humanity from the corruption and consequences of sin was made before he created the Universe.\n ( Ephesians 1:3-4 ,3:11 which speaks of God's eternal purpose historically accomplished by Jesus\n 2 Thessalonians 2:13 says that we were chosen for salvation from beginning .\n 2 Timothy 1:9,10) speaks of grace that was given to us before the beginning of time.\nEphesians 1:11 says that our redemption was determined before the creation of the world.\nin Ephesians 1:11,Romans 8:29,30 and Ephesians 1:5 the Greek word 'Proorizo' is used ,this term is most commonly translated as predestination .\nSo from above references we all agree that God's decision to save sinners was made as part of his eternal counsel, before the foundation of the world.	7	2020-05-22 23:46:06+05:30	2020-06-02 07:27:44+05:30	\N	452	796
1514	God's eternal plan of redemption involves the work of all three persons of the Trinity.\nTHE FATHER- originated the agreement because of his desire to redeem fallen human beings from the course of sin (Ephesians 3:10,11). According to Paul it was the Father's eternal purpose to accomplish our redemption through Christ.\nTHE SON- agreed to add a perfect human nature to his perfect divine nature to die on behalf of sinners.(2 Timothy 1:9) Paul said that we received grace in the Son before the beginning of time\nTHE HOLY SPIRIT agreed to enable and empower the Son's work and to apply salvation to those whom the Son redeemed .(2 Thessalonians 2:13)	6	2020-05-22 23:55:58+05:30	2020-06-02 07:27:44+05:30	\N	452	797
1515	COVENANT OF GRACE-The covenant relationship God established with humanity after our fall into sin that provides forgiveness and redemption on the basis of God's mercy in Christ\nFULFILLMENT-The covenant of grace fulfills part of God's eternal plan for history\nThe Father fulfilled his eternal decree in to covenant of grace by sending the Son and the/Spirit to work,appointing the son to the office of Messiah(John 5:36), giving the Son his powerful spirit without limit.( John 3:34),and preparing the Son's perfect human nature.\nThe Son fulfilled his eternal agreement to redeem humanity by veiling his divine glory, adding a full human nature, to his full divine nature,living a perfect life and dying an atoning death(Philippians 2:5-8)\nThe Holy Spirit fulfilled His part in God's eternal counsel by enabling and empowering the Son's incarnation and subsequent work, empowering Christ's death on the cross and his resurrection, regenerating our spirit, empowering us to resist sin ,giving us spiritual gift and securing our salvation	6	2020-05-23 00:07:55+05:30	2020-06-02 07:27:44+05:30	\N	452	798
1516	God the Son joined the covenant of grace as its mediator as\n1. He intercedes for God's covenant people\n2. He reconciles us to God by taking the blame and punishment for our sins\n3. He preserves the integrity of the covenant and the lives of his people by suffering the covenant curses and earning the covenant blessings\nThe Son began to mediate the covenant of grace when it was first made, back in the Garden of Eden ,when God first offered redemption to Adam and Eve. And He continues to mediate ever since.\nJesus ' role us our fully divine and fully human covenant mediator is what enabled him to atone for our sin  by dying in our place and because this solution to human sin will always be available in the covenant of grace, there will never be a need for divine providence to introduce another covenant, another covenant representative or another mediator.	8	2020-05-23 00:20:26+05:30	2020-06-02 07:27:44+05:30	\N	452	799
1517	ADMINISTRATIONS;\nThe covenant of grace was administered by various covenant representatives:\n1. ADAM-  The Adamic administration provided humanity the immediate opportunity to reconcile our relationships with God(Gen 4:25,26)\n2. NOAH- The Noahic administration expanded the covenant blessing by adding God's promise never again to destroy the earth with flood waters.\n3. ABRAHAM- In the Abrahamic administration the nation of Israel was charged with expanding God's kingdom throughout the earth (Romans 4:13)\n4. MOSES- In Mosaic administration God confirmed his promise to Abraham,provided structure fir the nation of Israel,gave Israel the first codified version of the law,redirected Israel t build his kingdom through out world .\n5. David-In the Davidic administration , the Mosaic administration was confirmed,it was revealed that the greatest covenant blessings would be fulfilled under the kingship of /David and his dynastic heirs.\n6. Jesus- In the New Covenant God established a permanent unbreakable covenant in which his people would receive all his covenant blessings.	8	2020-05-23 00:35:28+05:30	2020-06-02 07:27:44+05:30	\N	452	800
1518	Love consists of allegiance,action and affection\nAllegiance consists of :\nLOYALTY is the cornerstone of the concept of love. The most basic responsibility of the people is loyalty to the king.The suzerain's love was expressed legally in the form of covenant loyalty to his people:protection,justice,met needs.Vassal's love towards the king:obey,support and honor.\nJesus is our Lord and king and we are to render love to him through loyal obedience and loyalty to his church.\nORIENTATION;\nGod and his kingdom must be our highest priorities, the focus of our desire and the center of our world view.\nWhen we orient our lives around God and his people, we pursue the agenda of his kingdom and we are motivated ti love in ways that please him.\nRESPONSIBILITY\nOur loving allegiance to God should motivate us to seek out additional ways that we are responsible to him.When understanding that we are obligated to him in every area of our life, we are in a better position to make decisions that he approves.	8	2020-05-24 23:46:04+05:30	2020-06-02 07:32:05+05:30	\N	453	858
