1521	Yes I do remember when I was ten years old I came to saving faith, was not at all changed instantly at that moment , but gradually learnt His ways and followed His faith. This brings a great change in our motives and behaviors. it effects everything that we think about ourselves, our families ,our jobs , lour services and everything else in our lives.Is is an active faith that underlies and motivates our good works.Saving also involves our hearts, it is an inward disposition that cause us to think , speak and act in ways that please God . It involves mental,acts. so saving faith functions a as a motive in my life and enables me to do good works. Earlier my motives were selfish, self centered, but saving faith has influenced my motives and behaviors based on the love of God.	8	2020-05-25 00:17:07+05:30	2020-06-02 07:32:05+05:30	\N	453	861
1522	The term imagination refers to our ability to form mental image of thing that are beyond our experience.Imaginations are vital to learning and thinking about God , the world and our ourselves.\nCreativity:We can have good degree of confidence in our imagination when we use it carefully and rightly, because the Holy Spirit give  us this faculty as a reliable tool for assessing ethical knowledge\nTime:Bible requires us to pursue good goals especially the glorification of God through the triumph of his kingdom, but this goal is in the future. Without our ability to imagine the future ,we would not be able to apply God's word to our lives \nDistance:\nthe information we receive about the distant things is fallible, but we need to rely strongly on the Holy Spirit to help us evaluate our imagination.	8	2020-05-25 00:32:53+05:30	2020-06-02 07:32:05+05:30	\N	453	862
1523	Assessing knowledge means to evaluate the information we have received. Our intellect comes from God and His holy Spirit help us to use it rightly . It has an important role to play in our decision making process.\nReason is the capacity to make logical inferences and to judge logical consistency. It is also the ability to think and make judgement that accord with biblical patterns of thought.\nConscience: God given ability to discern good and evil. The solution to sin's corrupting influence is to rely on the power of the Holy Spirit who works within us as we strive to conform our conscience to God's word.\nEmotions are inner feelings , the effective aspects of our ethical sensitivity.\nWe must submit our emotions to the Holy spirit and Gods word and harmonize them with our other God given abilities and capacities.	8	2020-05-25 00:46:17+05:30	2020-06-02 07:32:05+05:30	\N	453	863
