1573	1. Kings- Kings were expected to protect and provide for their people, treat them with kindness, rule wisely to benefit their people. God is frequently presented as the suzerain or supreme emperor over all creation. God was king in a special way over Israel in the old testament and the church in the new testament.\n2. People- in old testament often Abraham and his descendants and in New testament generally the church. They populate the whole world, improve the world as Go had improved the Garden of Eden. God ruled directly over all humanity. He intended the world to be his kingdom. The people that God has called to himself; when God create the world, he set up humanity as his vassal kings. \n3. Covenants- God administered his kingdom through covenants. His covenants expressed God's goodwill toward his people , listed the people's obligations towards God, and stated the consequences of obedience and curses for disobedience.	8	2020-06-03 23:07:59+05:30	2020-06-16 03:50:58+05:30	\N	458	847
1552	The Ten Commandments have a special primacy over Scripture's other commandments. Historical and Theological.\nThe primacy of the Ten Commandments is both historical and theological. Their historical primacy depends on the fact that, to our knowledge, these laws were the first legal code that was received by Israel.\nBook of the Covenant: Additional laws received with the Ten Commandments. The Ten Commandments had theological or ideological primacy. God carved the ten commandments in the stone tablets. The giving of the Law was attended by thunder and lightning, smoke, clouds and heavenly trumpets. Moses identified the ten commandments as God's very covenant with his people. The Ten commandments were placed within the ark of the covenant. The laws listed by Jesus were from Leviticus 19:18 and summarizes the laws In short, Jesus indicated that by obeying ten commandments a person can earn eternal life. Even in the New testament the ten commandments were still spoken of in terms that reflected their theological primacy.	8	2020-05-30 23:01:43+05:30	2020-06-02 07:34:13+05:30	\N	457	839
1553	It is been common to categorize the various laws in the Old Testament, Bible into three major groups: moral law, ceremonial law and civil law. Moral laws are typically thought to convey God's ethical standards and are usually identified with the Ten Commandments. Civil Laws provide for the governing of society, especially during the period of Israel's theocracy. Ceremonial laws. in turn, are those which provide instruction for worshiping God. Frequently, these are most closely associated with the Old Testament sacrificial system, and tabernacle and temple administration. The existence of these categories, and the proper identification of laws, provides a mechanism by which they can avoid applying God's word to their lives. God's people are no longer to perform many of the specific behaviors that were required under the Mosaic sacrificial and temple system.	8	2020-05-30 23:08:33+05:30	2020-06-02 07:34:13+05:30	\N	457	840
1554	I would answer my friend by saying that the civil and ceremonial laws of the Old testament have expired in the sense that we are not to return to Old Testament patterns of life. In another sense, Old Testament civil and ceremonial laws still apply to modern Christians. Christians should still look to the civil and ceremonial laws of the Old testament, as well as to its moral laws for ethical guidance. Be it Old testament or New testament, the laws for man are needed for their social, cultural, and spiritual morality. Scripture teaches us the continuing application of every Old Testament law, and they help us to keep the good character and maintain it that we may lead a holy and God fearing life.	8	2020-05-30 23:18:05+05:30	2020-06-02 07:34:13+05:30	\N	457	841
1568	There are basic types of revelation; general revelation, which comes to us through the creation in general and existential revelation, which comes to us through persons, remember that God reveals his will to us in all three of these ways. Even though special, general, existential revelation differ in some respects, they all communicate content in the form of facts. These facts include everything that God reveals about our situation, such as events, people, objects, ideas, duties, actions- even God and his revelation. \nIt is possible to speak of the facts that God's revelation communicates in countless ways. In addition to speaking about facts in general, we will also speak of goals and means. Goals are the intended or potential outcomes of thoughts, words, and deeds. They include everything we  might think, say, or do, and any tool or method that we might use in order  to accomplish our objectives.	8	2020-06-03 22:16:10+05:30	2020-06-16 03:50:58+05:30	\N	458	842
1569	God is our ultimate fact, our ultimate ethical environment. In order for us to know our obligations before God, he must first reveal himself to us. God's character is our ultimate norm or standard. Correspondingly, from the situational, perspective, God is our ultimate fact, our ethical environment. The reality of God's existence rules over every ethical question and obligates us to live by the standard of his character. God is the supreme authority over all creation. His authority is absolute, and his character is the perfect expression of his will. So, when he reveals his character is the perfect expression of his will. So, when he reveals his character, that revelation is the means through which God exercises control much like human governments exercise control through their laws. And just as human beings obey civil laws because they bow to the government's authority, all creation must obey God's laws by bowing to his authority.	8	2020-06-03 22:25:15+05:30	2020-06-16 03:50:58+05:30	\N	458	843
1570	Goals- goal in ethics, we have in mind the expected outcomes of our endeavors. In many ways, this is no different from the way that we set goals to accomplish anything else in life. They can be things we hope to accomplish immediately, or things we plan to do in the distant future. Our goals give direction to our actions. Special, general, and existential revelation each teach us important generic facts, each type of revelation also provides us with goals that we must adopt in Christian ethics. Existential revelation also helps  us to discern good goals from evil goals, especially through our consciences. And in the case of believers, the Holy spirit is another source of existential revelation, moving within us so that we pursue good goals and shun evil ones.	7	2020-06-03 22:32:53+05:30	2020-06-16 03:50:58+05:30	\N	458	844
1571	The strategy of rigor results from mistaken beliefs about the Bible's similarity to modern world and about its clarity. This strategy gives little or no consideration to the ways that the facts, goals, and means of Scripture differ from those in the modern world. The strategies has some consequences too. Firstly, it destroys Christian freedom by prohibiting behaviors that are wrong under certain conditions, but good under other conditions. The classic example of this are Paul's discussions of food that had been sacrificed to idols in 1 Corinthians 8-10, and in Romans 14. \nSecond, a strategy of rigor also inspires despair in believers by turning God's word into a heavy burden. God gave his word to his people to bless them, not to oppress them. And there are many, many places in Scripture that state this idea. example is Mark 2;27 and in Romans 9;4,5. \nA good corrective is to realize  that modern situations are sufficiently different from biblical situations so that we cannot simply mimic the application we find in the scripture.	8	2020-06-03 22:49:30+05:30	2020-06-16 03:50:58+05:30	\N	458	845
1572	Jesus spoke about the kingdom of God in the sermon on the mount found in Mt 5-7. Three specific times when Jesus spoke of the kingdom of God as the goal of ethics during his sermon about earthly needs. In each of these sections, Jesus indicated that the kingdom of God must be the main priority of our lives. \n1. Beatitudes- Christian ethics- viewed as means of determining which human person, acts and attitudes receive God's blessing and which do not. So, which the beatitudes, Jesus began his Sermon by encouraging people to live ethically. Jesus set forth the blessings and ethics in terms of kingdom of God. Jesus specifically set forth the blessings of god's kingdom as the reward or goal that was to motivate his listeners to live ethically. \n2. Lord's Prayer- Jesus indicated that all creatures in heaven already obey God's will. but Jesus instructed us to pray that all creatures on earth would obey the divine king in the same way. \n3. Earthly needs- Jesus made it very plain that the ultimate goal of the christian life, the greatest end toward which we are to strive is the glorification of God through the triumph of his Kingdom.	9	2020-06-03 22:59:00+05:30	2020-06-16 03:50:58+05:30	\N	458	846
1574	Historical phases- creation; initial peace, fall- rebellion, redemption- final peace\n1. Initial peace- Adam and Eve were obedient servants. As a result, there was peace between God and humanity. All the components of the covenant worked properly to favor humanity. And at first, Adam and eve were blessed with close fellowship with God and continued to live in the Garden of Eden where life was easy and blissful.\n2. Rebellion- Humanity violated one of their covenant obligations. As a result, they received the covenant curses. Instead of turning to God in repentance and keeping our covenant obligations, we continued to rebel and to perpetuate the covenant curses. But God did not abandon us to rebellion and curse. Instead he determined to bring final peace to his kingdom and to return blessings to  his people.\n3. Final Peace- God began to restore peace to his kingdom immediately after humanity's fall into sin. Protoevangelion- God offered to send a redeemer to rescue humanity from the curse of sin. Therefore, God was working towards the goal of full redemption and success of his kingdom. But he did not restore his kingdom to the glory it had displayed during the initial peace days.	8	2020-06-03 23:20:08+05:30	2020-06-16 03:50:58+05:30	\N	458	848
