1600	Resurrection accomplished following things:\nGod 's anointed Christ conquered death for all of us, when he rose from the grace through the power of the Spirit,and he ensured the future resurrection and the blessing of all his faithful followers.\n1.  Plan of Redemption:\nGod planned to redeem humanity and the rest of the creation depended on him fulfilling his covenant promises,but he could not do it if Jesus remained dead.His resurrection was an affirmation of His role as Christ. Luke 24:45,46\nRedemption depended on God fulfilling His covenant promise to establish his kingdom on earth.\nBlessing of salvation:'\nBlessing we receive as part of our salvation are: \nJustification-which is the forgiveness of our sins Romans 4:25\nRegeneration of our spirits 1 Peter 1:3-5\neternal inheritance- it opens the door to our inheritance 1 Peter 1:3-5\nI produces good works and true witness and finally resurrection of believers.(2 Cor 4:10-18)	8	2020-06-14 00:32:51+05:30	2020-06-16 22:27:36+05:30	\N	464	769
1601	Jesus Christ is the most powerful .exciting person who has ever lived , what is more exciting is that he still lives today.He is our prophet, priest and king from his throne in heaven. And if we serve him faithfully, he assures us in his word that our blessings in the next world will be far beyond our greatest hopes. \nAs a minister of God , I face many challenges ,but Jesus has been my help and Christ and helped me overcome all tough circumstances.\nJesus is our great hope , and he will grant us the blessings of his kingdom. The vision of the future motivates me to serve God with a sense of urgency as we proclaim his gospel to the lost.\nThe return of Christ is the central affirmation OF Our Christian faith.\nAs in ministry , I face challenges from the enemy satan, Jesus governs all things and we know that the Bible assures us that because of Christ's rule over all,we have nothing to fear, our victory is sure. Nothing can happen to us that is beyond his control and authority. \nEven in our temptations since He is the Christ , HE is able to help us overcome those things.\nSo we affirm he is our Christ in all circumstances.	9	2020-06-14 00:51:52+05:30	2020-06-16 22:27:36+05:30	\N	464	770
1607	Ethics in general is to study on moral right and wrong, the study of good and evil.\nIn terms of Christian Theology, ethics is viewed as a means of determining how do we receive blessings based on human acts and attitudes.\n\nWhile studying Christian ethics we need to study on 2 important aspects\nGod's Divine Nature\nGod's Divine Actions \n\nGod's Divine Nature\nGod is not accountable to any standards outside of himself, and that everything that accords with God is good and light. \n\nScripture says in 1 John verse 5, that God is light and that there is no darkness in him.\n\nLight is considered as a metaphor of God, it is a moral evaluation and darkness is equated with Sin & Lies\n\nDivine Actions\nGod shows his approval for what is right by bestowing blessings. Similary God shows hatred for what is wrong and evil by withholding blessings and pouring out curses\n\nIn the old testament scriptures, God instructs the Israelites to strictly obey the commandments, on doing so - they would be blessed !!\nDisobedience would invite God's wrath, including death and destruction	0	2020-06-24 20:47:30+05:30	2020-06-24 20:47:30+05:30	\N	465	826
1608	Unless a work or action is performed with right motive, it is not a work that God will reward with blessings. Two important things that we need to always consider through our actions and works are \n1) Faith \n2) Love\n\nFAITH \nFaith plays a very important role in our life, any work done without a purified heart of faith is considered to be sinful and it does not please God. This criteria of the right motive is closely associated with good Christian Ethics.\n\nWorks of Faith can only be demonstrated by the indwelling of the Holy Spirit, and our actions and works accordingly  will culminate in rewards and blessings from God. Our faith should be consistent with growth, as it is also the means of purification within believers, motivating to produce good works.\n\nFaith without works is dead - as it says in the book of James, \nThe kind of faith that purifies the heart, faith that saves, faith that motivates to good works. \n\nIn the book of Hebrews it says, Without faith it is impossible to please God. \n\nUnless we try to please God and see blessings, our works and actions should be based on faith. \n\nAlso everything that is done without faith is considered to be sin, as instructed by Apostle Paul in the book of Romans.\n\nLOVE :\nApostle Paul says in 1st Corinthians 13 - Paul taught that our works are unproductive if it is not motivated by love. \n\nLove plays an important role in our Christian life, all our works and even spiritual gifts, for results to be evident should be motivated by love. Everything else will not receive the approval from our God.\n\nWhen Jesus spoke about the greatest commandment, it begins with Love\n\nLove the Lord your God with all your heart, and with all your soul and with all your mind.\n\nLove is an aspect of every law God requires us to obey. Love is the standard that God has set for maknkind to follow, wheter it is loving God or neighbor.	0	2020-06-24 21:04:51+05:30	2020-06-24 21:04:51+05:30	\N	465	827
1609	The threefold criteria for good works described in this lesson are as follows :\n\nAll our works should be based on \n1) Proper Motive\n2) Proper Standard \n3) Proper Goal\n\nProper Motive\nAll our works should have proper motive and it should be governed by two strong pillars of Faith & Love. Everything that we do, all our works if not done by faith & love will not be merited as per God's standards. The basic criteria for all our works to have a proper motive is Faith and Love\n\nProper Standard\nAll our works and actions should be of proper standard \nWestminster Confession of Faith says, that all our works that God commands, but unless done in a right manner according to the Word, they are sinful.\nAll sin violates God's law.\nIn order for our works to be of of proper standard it has to be governed by 3 aspects\n\n1) Commands of Scripture\nAll the commands of Scripture are designed to guide us. \n2) All of Scripture \nProper standard requires submission to the whole bible. God's word as a whole is a criterion for good works. \n3) General Revelation\nGod's revelation in creation itself is part of his word, that is commonly called as general revelation is also a standard for good works.\n\nGood works must conform to \nGod's Word - as Revealed in the Law, In all of Scriptiure and in General Revelation of Creation.	0	2020-06-24 21:22:37+05:30	2020-06-24 21:22:37+05:30	\N	465	828
1610	Perspectives are Ethical judgment involving the application of God's Word to a situation by a person. \nThe three different perspective to be emplyed when approaching ethics\n1) Situational Perspective\n2) Normative Perspective \n3) Existential Perspective\n\n1) Situational Perspective\nThis type of perspective focuses on the end or the result of actions. Always asking questions like, what are the best means of achieving God's purposes ? It also incudes appeals to moral behavior based on prior examples and other morally good characters as mentioned in the Scripture. We are to apply the scripture in our situations and follow the lead given in the word of God.\n\n2) Normative Perspective\nRefers to the fact that God's word is the norm or standard for ethics. We are doing ethics from normative perspecitve when we look at the word of God for directives as to what is to be done.\n\n3) Existential Perspecitve\nWhen we approach ethics by asking questions that are specific to the people involved, we are doing ethics from an existential perspective. It focuses on the self in confrontation and interaction with God.	0	2020-06-24 21:38:40+05:30	2020-06-24 21:38:40+05:30	\N	465	829
1611	God has the ultimate perogative to determind whether any particular action, emotions and thoughts meet or transgress his moral requirements and he has the ultimate right and power to act on his determinations. \n\nWhen we consider the scripture in the Gospel of John chapter 5, it says that \nMy judgement is just, for I seek not to please myself but him who sent me. \n\nGod in himself is the highest court in the universe. He will make the ultimate determination of wheterher or not we have lived morally or immorally and all his judgements will be true. No one can challenge his authority.  No one can challenge God's absolute authority, as it also follows absolute power. \n\nAs the absolute judge of morality, God consistently applies the absolute moral standard of his character in every judgement. His judgements are perfect, exhibiting flawless insight and wisdom.	0	2020-06-24 21:49:08+05:30	2020-06-24 21:49:08+05:30	\N	465	830
1612	The three categories of revelation that are part of God's Word are as follows :\n1) Special Revelation \nSpecial revelation is made up of Scripture, prophecy, dreams and visions\nThe complexity of speical revelation is that it come in various forms. It involves God communicating with people in ways that transcend the normal ways of creation. \nIn some cases God appears visibly, whereas in some cases speaks audibly to groups or individuals. In other cases he speaks through an angel. God also provides special revelation to write down and recorded in Scripture.  These types of special revelation are very special as they represent the extraordinary or supernatural communication between God and man. \n\n2) General Revelation :\nGeneral Revelation is what happens in history, in the universe, weather, plants, animals and human beings\nIt speaks about the way creation and history tell us true things about God and his moral requirements, But due to the fall of Adam and Eve, and the fallen world, the General Revelation does not present us with a clear picture of God's character. But the Bible assures us that general revelation still speaks clearly enough to teach us true things about God.\n\n3) Existential Revelation \nGod reveals himself in and through persons has always been recognized as a part of general revelation. \nIt can be further divided into External and Internal aspects\nExternal includes the revelation through human beings, created in the image og God. Human beings reflect God;s glory and dignity. Our image reflects God's character. \n\nInternal : \nInternal types of existential revelation involves the Holy Spirit working within human beings to reveal truth about God. Divine gifts that form part of this revelation in enabling to grow spritiually.	0	2020-06-24 22:09:00+05:30	2020-06-24 22:09:00+05:30	\N	465	831
1613	When God created man in his own image , God had given Adam exercising authority. When Adam named the animals he was thinking and exercising the divinely delegated authority, whenever human beings think and judge in an exercisde we are reflective God's character.\n\nSimilary Jesus has also taught in the Scripture - where every matter may be established by the testimony of two or three witnesses.\n\nJesus supports their exercise of the authority that he has delegated the church.\n\nInternal Existential Revelation talks about the ways that the Holy Spirit works with human beings to reveal truth about God.\nTheologians consider 2 important topics\nIllumination & Inward leading of the Holy Spirit \n\nIllumination of the Holy Spirit, is a divine gift of understanding that God gives to believers and even to unbelievers. Whe Holy Spirit illuminates a person's mind the ability or knowledge of that person increases and he is able to grasp information that he previously lacked. \n\nInward Leading - is one of the most common ways in which Holy Spirit works within individuals to reveal truth about God's character. We see inward leading displayed clearly in our individual consciences and as well in our feelings that God would provide us while taking a particular course of action. \n\nIn all these things God's character or standard is revealed unto us as we consistently study the scriptures.	0	2020-06-24 22:27:03+05:30	2020-06-24 22:27:03+05:30	\N	465	832
1614	1st John 1: 7 says that \nBut if we walk in the light as He is in the light, we have fellowship with one another and the blood of Jesus Christ His Son cleanses us from all sin. \n\nOur commitments and submission to the calling in full obedience, enables us to have fellowship with our Lord, and also the fellowship with our co-believers. \n\nThe moment that we receive forgiveness for all our sins, as the blood of Jesus cleanses us from all our sins, automatically we become part and parcel of the divine calling and standards that God has set for us. Our Lord who is the source of light, enables us to walk in the light leaving aside all works of darkness that is equated with sin and lies. Our daily lifestyles should reflect the character, standards and values based on God's word. Whether in our personal lives in front of others. Our inward desire and hunger and calling should all match the calling and purpose as revealed through the scrip	0	2020-06-24 22:47:06+05:30	2020-06-24 22:47:06+05:30	\N	465	833
1615	The Bible relates the true story of creation in order to explain how humanity was actually designed to function within the world. Many other parts of the Bible appeal to the creation accounts to prove how the world supposed to work and what role human beings are morally obligated to play. CREATION ORDINANCES ARE MORAL REQUIREMENTS ESTABLISHED BY GOD'S WORKS OF CREATION.God's works are perfect , and therefore, they are the standard for our own behavior. Sometimes creation ordinances are explicit, such as God's command to be fruitful and multiply in Genesis 1:28.\n But others are implicit such as our obligation to keep the sabbath holy.\nBut in the Ten Commandments ,in  Exodus 20:11, Moses clarified that God's pattern of working six days and resting on the seventh obligated human beings to do the same.	9	2020-06-24 23:14:37+05:30	2020-06-26 03:23:53+05:30	\N	467	589
1616	The book of Genesis contains two accounts of creation .One is in Genesis 1:1-2:3 and other is in Genesis 2:4-25.\nGENESIS 1:1-2:3\nGod spent six days forming and filling the universe:\nDay 1:God separated dark from light.\nDay 2: God separated the waters above from the waters below\nDay 3: God separated dry land and sea.\nDay 4: God filled the light and darkness with heavenly bodies(sun, moon ,stars)\nDay 5: God filled the sky and oceans with birds and sea creatures.\nDay 6:God filled the dry land with animals and created human beings to rule over creation\nFocus:\nhuman beings were created in God's image and given authority over creation \nSecond account:\nGenesis 2:4-25\nThis account contains more details to God's work on the sixth day\na.God formed the animals from the dust of the earth\nb. God made the first man from the dust of the earth and breathed life into him.\nc.Adam looked for a  suitable helper from among the animals\nd. God created Eve, the first woman from Adam's rib\nEve  was under Adam's authority in their marriage , but she was equal to him in the tasks God assigned to them as a  race.	8	2020-06-24 23:28:59+05:30	2020-06-26 03:23:53+05:30	\N	467	590
1617	Adam and Eve were created superior to the rest of God's earthly creatures in following ways:\n1.Created on the sixth day, separately from the animals ,as the culmination of creation (Gen 1:27)\n2. God called them "very good".\n3. Only Adam is said to have his life breathed into him by God(2:7)\n4. God created them in His image and appointed them to rule over creation on his behalf (Genesis 1:27-28, Psalms 8:6-8)\nGod created humanity to reflect his glory and his attributes in ways that other creatures couldn't.\nBecause human beings are likenesses of God.\na.Our existence points to his power and goodness\nb. no other creature carries this much honor and inherent dignity\nHumanity also has a superior role to administer God's rule over the earth (Genesis 2:20)	8	2020-06-24 23:38:25+05:30	2020-06-26 03:23:53+05:30	\N	467	591
1618	Some common beliefs that exist in our culture regarding human origins are  evolution theory, molecular theory , big bang theories.\nEvolution theories of Charles Darwin says that human beings were developed gradually from human ancestors which resembled  apes and similar creatures.\nBut Bible says that human beings were created the sixth day by God Almighty in His own image and likeness. The human that we see was not a gradually developed or evolved organism but we were purposefully and intentionally created by God as per His divine will.\nOther theory is some sort of molecular evolution , the proteins of our DNA and DNAs of other creatures were gradually developed as species and genes\nBut in the contrary Bible says that human beings and all other creatures were created according to their respective features and characteristics of their own  , each different in species and genes.	8	2020-06-24 23:49:05+05:30	2020-06-26 03:23:53+05:30	\N	467	592
1619	Adam and Eve did the works of the priests in the garden of Eden.Humanity is still responsible to God for fulfilling the moral obligations that flow from Adam's priestly duties  .\nPriestly obligations:\nWe fulfill it in our lives by serving God and worshiping him.  We cultivate and guard the creation . \n Being in full time ministry , we try our best to train others too to urn the world into a sanctuary that is fitting for God's purpose. We begin it with our home. We try to carry the same attitude in our local church too.\nIn the church ministry and our home too, in every opportunity of our lives we consider it our priority to render the sacrifices of praise and obedience to him. We try to fulfill the mission of reconciliation of others to God , by proclaiming hid goodness, salvation and forgiveness to the world.\nRoyal obligations:\nGod commanded Adam and Eve to increase the human race in order to spread its rule over the whole world. This task falls especially on God's faithful people in the church. So we as ministering family try our best by sharing his love to others and reaching out to others and turning the entire planet into God's earthly sanctuary as an extension of his heavenly kingdom .	9	2020-06-25 00:05:14+05:30	2020-06-26 03:23:53+05:30	\N	467	801
1620	To understand historical analysis we need to review some broad perspectives  that Holy Spirit has led the church to pursue the exegesis of Scripture in three ways :\nliterary analysis, historical analysis, thematic analysis\nHistorical analysis looks at scripture as a window to history, exploring historical events lying behind the Bible. It is especially concerned with the "acts of God".\nBiblical theology approaches the Scripture primarily with historical analysis. It looks at the Bible as a window that gives access to history. In this the focus of exegesis shifts from traditional theological themes to the historical events described in the Bible ,a very different set of priorities and concerns emerge. While sound Biblical theology is based on historical analysis of the Scriptures , we should turn to the fact that it is primarily concerned with the acts of God.	8	2020-06-25 23:46:47+05:30	2020-06-26 03:23:03+05:30	\N	468	655
1621	Historical analysis can take different forms  of at least two main tendencies:\nFACTUAL HISTORICAL ANALYSIS AND THEOLOGICAL HISTORICAL ANALYSIS\nThese two tendencies go hand in hand , but their main concerns are quite different\nA factual approach to historical analysis is concerned with questions like the date f the exodus under Moses, the historical circumstances that gave rise to Israel's monarchy , evidences certain battles and other crucial events. The goal of factual historical analysis is rather straight forward.\nTheological historical analysis-\nIt is  the theological significance of the acts of God reported in Scripture.\nChristians tend to agree with Aquinas that theology has two main concerns:\nOn the one hand a theological matter is anything that refers directly to God . And on the other hand a theological matter is anything that describes other subjects in relation to God.The former category is what traditional theology calls theology proper And the latter category includes matter such as doctrines of humanity, sin salvation ,ethics , church and the like	9	2020-06-26 00:03:49+05:30	2020-06-26 03:23:03+05:30	\N	468	656
1622	The shifts in culture that accompanied the rise of biblical theology are as follows:\n1. Biblical theology is in large measure a response to cultural shifts that can be traced back to the enlightenment of the 17th century\n2.Biblical theology is a christian response to a prominent intellectual movement in the modern period often called modern historic ism .It is the belief that history holds the key for understanding ourselves and the world around us.\n3. The German philosopher George Wilhelm Friedrich Hegel is best known for his proposal that every aspect of reality is caught up in logical patterns of historical progress known as dialectic.\n4.  This and other forms of historic ism rose to prominence in the modern period for many reasons . For instance a) archaeology\nb)geology\nc)biology\nd)and every academic discipline including theology.	8	2020-06-26 00:14:59+05:30	2020-06-26 03:23:04+05:30	\N	468	657
1623	Gabler spoke that systematic theology was not to examine or explain the Bible, but to determine what Christians should believe in the modern world through rational reflection on science and religion.As a critical theologian Gabler believed that the Christians should believe only those parts of the Bible that pass the standards of modern rational and scientific analysis.\nIt became increasingly difficult for critical theologians to draw from the scriptures as they formed their systematic theology. We might have expected them simply to set aside \nbiblical theology since they thought the Bible was riddled with misleading historical claims . And this has been the reactions of many during the modern period . But the field of Biblical theology did not die when  critical  theologians rejected biblical authority , instead they found other ways to use Scriptures for contemporary theology. Instead of teaching the Bible as true history, they began to look at the Scriptures as expressions of ancient religious sentiments presented as historical claims and they explored how these ancient religious feelings and experiences might be useful to modern Christians . So they have come to approach the Scriptures through Biblical theology	8	2020-06-26 00:31:09+05:30	2020-06-26 03:23:04+05:30	\N	468	658
1624	The divine goal of all world history is the extension of God's perfect heavenly reign to every corner of the earth.When God's will is done as perfectly on earth as it is in heaven, at that time the ultimate goal of history will be fulfilled. The opening chapter of the Bible describes the way God began to turn the chaotic world into his kingdom by ordering creation and placing his image in the garden of Eden but humanity rebelled and brought corruption and death in to the world.\nThe rest of the Old Testament reports how God Israel as his special people, God accomplished much through Israel but Israel also failed miserably.\nDespite these failures, God did not give upon Hid grand purpose. AS the New testament reveals God sent His eternal Son into the world and through His death God redeemed  a people for himself.Through Christ's resurrection and ascension , the ministry of the Holy Spirit, His glorious return, Christ is completing  the task originally given to humanity.\nRevelation 11:15\nChrist is hailed as the one who will bring God's  kingdom on earth.\nIn this approach to biblical theology. every event in biblical history is part of this grand scheme, while the Goal of biblical history is to bring God glory by establishing his worldwide kingdom in Christ	8	2020-06-26 00:47:04+05:30	2020-06-26 03:23:04+05:30	\N	468	659
