1647	The word"synchronic " derives from two Greek words :the preposition sun which means 'with' or 'together with' and the noun chronos which means 'time'.When the word synchronic is applied to historical events ,it describes occurrences that took place "together in time" or "at the same time".\nIllustration:\nwhen movie directors tell their stories . they convey a flow of events from beginning to end. They depict how one event leads to another and another and so on. Yet. even though the movie is one , whole unit is also broken down into smaller parts called scenes. Each scene tells a portion of the larger story . In this scene, each scene represents a synchronic moment in the movie , a period of time in the film.\nIn Synchronic synthesis , biblical theologians concentrate their attention on particular periods of time in the Old Testament. It's important to realize like scenes in a movie , synchronic approaches can focus on periods of various lengths. Sometimes biblical theologians focus on relatively brief historical moments, but other moments they concern themselves with relatively long periods of time  .	8	2020-06-30 23:55:23+05:30	2020-07-01 19:47:44+05:30	\N	481	660
