1755	God's authority :\nGod's authority in ethics is absolute. His moral judgements, his outlook on good and evil. God alone holds ultimate authority, and is always superior to all other authority.  God's authority is exhaustive, it extends to everything he has created in detail. All humans are accountable to God irrespective of their culture or religion. Everything in creation functions as God wants it to and is therefore good. Everything else against is considered to be evil.\n\nGod's Control :\nChristianity has always affirmed that God is the creator and he exercises sovereign control over his creation. This has been the basis for ethical responsibility. We are to live morally and reverently becaus God is working in our lives, causing to will and to act according to his plan. God orders creation, our circumstances are never an excuse to our unethical choices. \n\nGod's Presence :\nGod is omnipresent, hence us judges us on the basis of what he sees. Our ethical decisions must always account for God's presence with us as a royal judge to be always considered as we make ethical decisions.\nJesus earthly presence also provides us with the supreme pattern of righteousness for all human life. \nHoly spirit bestows gifts for our spiritual growth & obligates us to identify and use the gifts that God has given us.	0	2020-08-05 20:50:46+05:30	2020-08-05 20:50:46+05:30	\N	506	850
1744	The Apostle's Creed is foundational to theology because it introduces us to the teachings of apostles recorded in scripture. \n1. Standard- The apostles' creed functions as a doctrinal standard because it presents several of the biggest most important ideas of Christianity. These ideas are taught so clearly in Scripture that they should be recognized and embraced by everyone. Using the creed as a standard helps us remain faithful to scripture when convincing false teachers present us with bad theology. So, it helps to have a short list of essential beliefs that can anchor us to the teachings of Scripture and the apostles' creed provides such an anchor. \n2. Logical Basis- Logically basic ideas are the sources of other ideas. The creed provides the big doctrines so we can: see the relationship between the different beliefs in our theological systems. Doctrines that are more remote from Scripture in ways that harmonize with our fundamental beliefs helps us remain faithful to scripture.	8	2020-08-01 21:44:40+05:30	2020-08-05 04:03:46+05:30	\N	507	870
1756	Preternatural realm is inhabited by invisible spirits such as angels and demons. Angels and demons have a significant impact that happens in real life. Preternatural world is an important consideration when it comes to making ethical decisions.\n\nAs we study the scripture, it teaches us that God has also populated the universe with a vast number of spiritual persons known as angles and demons. They both are considered to be rational beings that have wills and personalities.\n\nWhen God created angles, they were pure and perfect serving God in heaven. But some of the angels rebelled against God and were removed from their blessed estate to being condemned. \n\nAngles serve as God's loyal messengers and agents. They communicate God's word to human beings, and they interact with humanity on God's behalf, Angelse are also known as ministering spirits sent to serve those who will inherit salvation. \n\nDemons are also able to interact with the natural realm, but they do in order to harm us.  Demons constantly tempt us trying to lead us away from moral choices\n\nInteractions / Spiritual Warfare :\n\nEver since Satan and his demons rebelled against God, they have been locked in spiritual battle against God's holy angels. \n\nAs Apostle Paul teaches us in the book of Ephesians, our enemies include the demonic rulers, authorities, powers and forces in the preternatural world. It also allows and influences us in ethical ways, as angels help us find ways to obey god, whereas demons tempt us to sin.\n\nThough Jesus has already crippled demon's ability to overtake us through his death and resurrection. but still demons persist in skirmishes against us, as a result we always need to be vigilant and ready for battle, relying on the armor of God and his grace to take a stand against evil forces.	0	2020-08-05 21:08:17+05:30	2020-08-05 21:08:17+05:30	\N	506	851
1757	Natural World includes\n1) Creation - original condition\n2) Fall - of humanity into sin\n3) Redemption - of humanity from sin\n\nCreation : \nWhen we study the book of Genesis, Moses described the creation of the entire natural realm in a way that emphasized the central importance of huanity over the earth.\nHuman beings are a part of nature\nGod created us from the dust of the ground\nWe have an ethical obligation to protect nature\nHuman beings are lords or rules over nature, to have dominion over all of God's creation, to rule, administer, to govern - to promote life and growth and turning this world into a kingdom that is fit to inhabit.\n\nFall : \nAfter the sin of Adam & Eve, God cursed both the human race, the earth and subjected it to corruption. Causing the earth to oppose the lordship of humanity.\nIt became difficult for humans to work and produce food.\nNature too is a recipient and instrument in God's curses\nNature is not as it was originally designed it often complicated our ethical decisions since it is corrupted by sin.\n\nRedemption :\nRedemption reversed the curses on the natural realm. Natural realm became an instrument of redemption\nGod purges corruption of the natural world through redemption of humanity.\nGod uses things in the natural realm as tools in the redemptive process\nEvents in the natural world testify to God's greatness\nGod will refine both heaven and earth to create a new heaven and a new earth\nThe corruption of natural world will last until humanity's redemption is completed at Christ's return.	0	2020-08-05 21:26:41+05:30	2020-08-05 21:26:41+05:30	\N	506	852
