1750	God as he is presented in scripture by looking at two subjects. The ''singularity'' of God, the fact that he is the only God that exists. And the ''simplicity'' of God, noting that he really is only one God, despite the fact that he has three persons. \n1. Polytheism- Belief in the the existence of multiple Gods. In polytheism, no one God can claim to be the only supernatural being who exercises control over the universe. One reason for this was so common that polytheism was often required by law.\n2. Monotheism- Belief in only one God. Scripture asserts that there is only one God- 1 Kings 8.60- The Lord is God...there is no other. Psalms 86.10- You alone are God. \n3. Christianity- The creed does not explicitly say that there is only one God. It is organized around a Trinitarian Formula. It indicates that the God of Christianity is the only one who deserves to be called "God."	8	2020-08-04 21:10:53+05:30	2020-08-05 04:02:44+05:30	\N	510	871
