1784	The Holy Spirit is identified as the Spirit of God's son is Galatians 4.6, and as the Spirit of the Father in Matthew 10. 20. And he has several other names that highlight the relational connections between the members of the Trinity. The distinction between the Spirit and the other persons of the Trinity is not always entirely clear. \nDistinctions between the Spirit and the other persons of the Trinity: distinctions between the Spirit and the other persons of the Trinity is to look at passages in Scripture that show them interacting with one another in ways that emphasize their differences. There are many passages that show these distinctions, but two passages will suffice to show that the Spirit is distinct from the Son and from the Father. As consider Jesus' words in John 16. 7; I tell you the truth, it is for good that I am going away. Unless I go away, the counselor will not come to you, but if I go, I will send him to you. \nalso in John 16. 7 the spirit would not begin until the Son had completely his earthlyd into heaven. This makes it clear that Spirit is distinct from the Son.\nHoly Spirit intercedes on our behalf with the Father, he demonstrated that they are distinct persons- one interceding and other hearing the interceding.	7	2020-08-11 21:48:07+05:30	2020-08-14 09:32:30+05:30	\N	517	884
1785	There are two perspectives: \nOntological Trinity- We are focusing on God's being and existence. From this perspective, the Holy Spirit is equal in power and glory to the Father and the Son. All three of God's persons are infinite, eternal and unchangeable. and each has the same essential divine attributes such as wisdom, power, holiness, justice, goodness and truth. \nEconomic Trinity- we are considering how God's persons interact with each other. From this perspective, each person of the GodHead has different responsibilities, different authority and a different assigned role. The Spirit's authority is subject to higher authority of the Father and the Son. and the Spirit's role is largely to carry out their instructions and to bring them glory. The Holy Spirit is called the third person of the Trinity.	7	2020-08-11 21:54:44+05:30	2020-08-14 09:32:30+05:30	\N	517	885
1796	Love is central to Bible's teaching, we are exhorted to love the Lord and also to love each other. \n\nLoyalty is the cornerstone of the concept of love. \nIn the Old Testament period, God is our king and he rules over us, Suzerain love was expressed largely in the form of covenant loyalty to his people. We are bound in covenant with God. The most important way we can show our love form him is through our earnest covenant loyalty\nIn the New Testament - Jesus is our Lord and King, and we are to render love to him through loyal obedience.\nWe cannot place other loyalties ahead of our loyalty to him. \nLoyalty is a positive virtue, motivating us to serve our Lord and King\n\nOrientation:\nOur lives must be comprehensively oriented around God. God and his kingdom should be our highest priorities, our focus and our desires should revolve around God. Scripture teaches us to be fully committed to God and his people.\nThe prime example for proper orientation is the life of Jesus. \nJesus life revolved around God and the people he came to save. This orientation motivated him to obey God perfectly in all things.\n\nResponsibility\nOur loving submission to God should motivate us to seek out additional ways that we are responsible to him.\nSeeking our reponsibilities before God, provides us unlimited allegiance to God.\nUnderstanding that we are obligated to God in every area of our life, we are in a better position to make decision that God approves.	0	2020-08-19 20:46:04+05:30	2020-08-19 20:46:04+05:30	\N	518	858
