1837	The threefold criteria  to good works are :\nObedience to God's command must be done with the proper motive , second it must be dine according to the proper standard and third it must be dine with the proper goal in mind  to glorify God.\nProper Motive:\nUnless a work is done with the right motive, it is not a work that god will reward with blessings. First kit must proceed from a heart that is purified by faith. Second actions must flow out of Christian love.\nProper Standard :\nBesides pointing that good works must flow from the right motives, the Westminister Confession of faith also states that good works must conform to the right standard In order for works to be good, they must be done according to the standard of the word of God , i.e God's revelation in the form of commands of Scripture, all of scripture and third general revelation, creation itself.\nProper Goal:\nAll good works must have the right end or goal.\nEven in our immediate gals like caring for our families , obeying our parents, our core we want to glorify God, by living in a way that please him.	8	2020-08-28 23:47:28+05:30	2020-09-08 06:04:30+05:30	\N	527	828
