1860	The old testament bible into three main types :\nMoral Law, ceremonial law and civil law \nMoral laws are typically thought to convey God's ethical standards and are usually identified with the ten commandments.\nCivil laws provide for the governing of society, especially during the Israel's theocracy.\nCeremonial laws are those which provide instruction for worshiping God.\nSince death , burial, resurrection and ascension of Christ , God's people are no longer  to perform many of the specific behavior that were required under the Mosaic sacrificial an temple system.. We are no longer  to maintain the temple or to restrict human and Gentiles from access to God's holy presence or to sacrifice animals for our sin,. Christ fulfilled the ceremonial  aspects of the law. We are to follow them by trusting Christ as our sacrifice and by worshiping him by spirit and truth.\nChrist fulfills the civil aspect of the law, but we live rightly under respective earthly governments and also directly honoring Christ as a king and by keeping his commandments.\nChrist fulfills the moral aspects of the law, we must also conform ourselves to Christ;s image and example seeking to live as morally as He did.	9	2020-09-02 00:54:21+05:30	2020-09-12 08:44:38+05:30	\N	530	840
