1885	There are three main components of the Kingdom of God. They are \n1. King-\nGod is the ruler of this kingdom, but since we haven't lived under a king , its difficult to understand the authority of a human king.\nIn the ancient world of the Bible, people were very familiar with kings and kingdoms. They were to protect  and provide for them , and to treat them with kindness. Good kings ruled wisely to benefit their people.God's supreme rule as the king over all is a major theme that runs throughout the Bible.\n\n2. People-\nThe bible speaks about the people of God's kingdom , it is referring to the people that God has called him to himself in contrast  to the people pf the world who follow the ways of evil.\n'In the Old testament it was about Abraham and his descendants.\nIn New Testament, it is about the Church, since Christians of all races have been adopted in to family of Abraham's family in Christ\n3. Covenants-\nThroughout the Bible . God administered his Kingdom through covenants.\nIt expressed God's good will towards his people, blessings for obedience and curses for disobedience,.\nThese covenants are Adamic, Noahic, Abrahamic, Mosaic, Davidic and New Covenant.\nBiblical covenants indicates the facts of our situation that God is our kings and that we are his kingdom servants	9	2020-09-08 00:30:33+05:30	2020-09-08 06:07:00+05:30	\N	532	847
