2117	In his mercy God was not willing to let entire humanity to remaining under the curse of the sin, he still planed for the humanity to fill and rule over the earth, and turn it to the kingdom worthy of his presents , so he send a redeemer to solve the problem of sin, and the redeemer was his son, Jesus Christ .\n    as a work of divine grace , forgiveness involves all three person of trinity , the father , the son, and the holy spirit , \n   Forgiveness being with the father because he was one that planned , the new testament explicitly teach us that the father sent the son in to the world and appointed him as the redeemer , the new testament also teaches that the father authorized the Jesus's empowerment as the redeemer of his people , as promised to accept Jesus sacrifice on the cross as payment of sin,\n  The divine grace that accomplished our forgiveness also involved the son, whom is our redeemer ,the fulfilment of the father promise , the son was sent into the world , become incarnate as Jesus as long awaited messiah , in order to atone for human sin, Jesus atoned for sin by dying on the cross in place of sinners , he received the divine curs that had been warrened by our sin, and his perfect righteousness was credited to our account , so that we would be continued not as sinners , but as obedient children of God.\n   The holy spirit is the person of trinity who actully applies the forgivness to our lives , the father laid the plans the son accomlished the atonement ,but our sins are not forgiven until the holy spirit dose his work,.	7	2020-10-30 07:05:59+05:30	2020-11-05 23:40:39+05:30	\N	577	892
2118	Scripture clearly taches us that God dose not forgive the sin of every person, some people are forgiven ad some are not, from the human perspective the reason is that the porous of forgiveness ordinarily involves and element of individual responsibility , generally spiking those people that fulfill these responsibilities are forgiven but those that shirk these responsibilities are not, \nscripture speak abut the two conditions for the forgiveness , in scripture faith is multifaceted concept but this context when we speak of faith in God , we have in mend, acknowledgement of God's divine sovereignty loyal submission to him, and trust that he will show us mercy for sake of our redeemer Jesus Christ, \nsome times Christian fall into distinguish between a means of grace and a basis of grace , as result they mistakenly think that means of grace can be used to earn grace ,or even to force God to be gracious to us , so its important to distinguish clearly between a means and a basis ,we might summarize these different by saying that a basis is the ground or merit on which an action or consequents is based , where as means is a tool or mechanism for bringing that action or consequence to pass .	7	2020-10-30 07:23:24+05:30	2020-11-05 23:40:39+05:30	\N	577	893
