2135	The redemption of our body is in three stage: Present life, intermediate state and  new life:\nPresent Life:\nBible teaches that the salvations of our bodies begins with the indwelling of the holy spirit, when we first come to faith, Romans 8:9-11. it does not result bin our immediate bodily resurrections , it does seal us with the guarantee of the full redemption of the bodies in the future. Ephesians 1:13-14\nintermediate state: the holy spirit sets us apart for God and purifies us to the sanctification\nIntermediate state:\nwhen we die, our bodies are temporarily separated from our soul , this stage is often called the intermediate state. the state between our live s on earth now  and the lives we will have in the resurrection. during the intermediate state our souls dwell with Christ in heaven\nMathew 17:3\nNew Life: Our bodies will receive new perfect life when they are restored to life in the general resurrections. in the resurrection the consequences if sin will , finally and forever be put away from us. Romans 8:23\nJust Christ bodies under went changes  in the resurrection, our bodies will also be changed, they will be renewed and perfected .they will be immortal, glorious, powerful and spirit-full.	8	2020-11-04 00:14:03+05:30	2020-11-05 23:39:19+05:30	\N	582	895
