2180	The book of Genesis contains two accounts of Creation\n\nThe First Creation Account : (Genesis 1:1-2:3)\nThe first creation account, we are told that creation was originally formless and empty. \n\nFirst three days God dealt with the fact that the earth was formless and started giving shape to it's various realms. Earth was void and without shape, God separated dry land from the seas.\n\nNext 3 days, God dealt with the fact that creation was empty and he started filling it wity light, birds and animals\nOn the 6th day, God created man in His own image, and gave him authority over his other creatures.\n\nThe Second Creation Account (Genesis 2:4-25) \nMentions about God's work on the sixth day, when he created the land animals and humanity.\n\nGod created the animals from the dust of the earth. Only Adam received the breath from God. \n\nAdam named all the aimals and this demonstrated his authority over them. God created the first woman Eve from Adam's rib. Both were created in God's image and were asked to fill and subdue the earth. \n\nOnly man had the authority to rule as representatives of God in this earth.	8	2020-11-12 04:59:09+05:30	2020-11-16 21:17:49+05:30	\N	593	590
