2207	The Kingdom of God, also called Kingdome of Heaven, is Christianity, the spiritual realm over which God reigns as king, or the fulfillment of Earth of God's will.  The phrase occurs frequently in the New Testament, primarily used by Jesus Christ in the first three Gospels. It is generally considered to be the central theme of Jesus' teaching, but widely differing views have been held about Jesus teaching on the Kingdom of God and its relation to the developed view of the church. \n\nAccording to the first three Gospels, most of Jesus' miraculous actions are to be understood as prophetic symbols of the coming of the Kingdom, and his teaching was concerned with the right response to the crisis of its coming. The nationalistic tone of much of the Jewish expectation is absent from the teaching of Jesus.	9	2020-11-18 10:58:46+05:30	2020-11-29 11:22:44+05:30	\N	600	848
2208	In the Old Testament, the law can be understood in 3 dimensions: Ceremonial, civil, and moral. God's laws were given to help people love God with all their hearts and minds. When Jesus talked about a new way to understand God's law, he was actually trying to bring people back to its original purpose. Jesus did not speak against the law itself but against the abuses and excesses to which it had been subjected.\n\nChristians have typically insisted that the moral aspects of the Torah remain relevant for example, the Ten Commandments, but not the ceremonial, legal, or ritualistic aspect. But it is necessary to keep in mind that this material is Scripture. Throughout its long history, the Church has taught that the meaning of scripture is never exhausted by a literal or historical reading.	8	2020-11-18 11:09:46+05:30	2020-11-29 11:22:44+05:30	\N	600	849
2214	Ethics is the science of morality. Its task is to examine the moral aspect of human nature and behavior, to clarify issues in moral decision making and moral dilemmas, and to facilitate the formation of moral character.  In Micah 6:8 we find a helpful definition of morality. It can be argued on the information found in that passage that morality asks four questions. Not what is normal, legal, or acceptable in a given culture, but what is good. Human beings are born with the rights, to which they have God-given rights. Immoral conduct consists of denying these rights to our fellow human beings. Our relationships and our inter-human conduct must be kind and compassionate.	7	2020-11-26 08:42:43+05:30	2020-11-29 11:24:26+05:30	\N	601	850
2215	In some ways, making biblical decisions requires to identify many factual details. And we also have to figure out how all these facts related to the ethical questions. Throughout many studies, biblical decisions have been that ethical judgement involves the application of God's word to a situation by a person.  This outlook on ethics has reminded us there are three major perspectives to be taken on every ethical issue. A focus on God's word, which we have called the normative perspective; a focus on the person, which we have called the existential perspective; and a focus on the situation, which we have called the situation perspective.  The importance of considering facts about God, the world around us and human beings when we make ethical decisions.	7	2020-11-26 08:59:02+05:30	2020-11-29 11:24:26+05:30	\N	601	851
