2281	The Bible relates the true story of creation in order to explain how humanity was actually designed to function within the world. The Bible contain the appeal to the creation accounts to prove how the world is supposed to work and what role human beings are morally obligated to play. \nTheologians often refer these obligations as ' creation ordinances'. They are moral requirements established by God's work of creation.\nSome times, creation ordinances are explicit. For example; God's command to be fruitful and to multiply is very vivid. It is a direct command to the human beings. But there are implicit ordinances like' keeping Sabbath day holy. The creation accounts don't say explicitly about keeping Sabbath. But in Exodus 20:11, Moses clarified that God's pattern of working six days and resting on the seventh. \nThus the creation ordinances shed light on the rules and obligations for the function of creation on this earth. Violation of them will lead to Chaos and calamity.	8	2020-12-18 15:12:10+05:30	2021-01-09 20:20:00+05:30	\N	617	589
2282	The two accounts of creation ( Genesis 1:1-2:3 and 2:4-25)give us a general picture of how and why we are created. Both these accounts compliment each other. The first narrative give a picture of the whole creation process when the second is the kind of a window to the sixth day of creation. \nIn the first account we see God giving form and shape to the formless and empty universe. First three days God did it by separating light and darkness, forming sky and the atmosphere and finally separating dry land and water. Next three days God filled the sky with heavenly bodies like sun, moon and stars on fourth day; birds in the sky and sea creatures on fifth day and on sixth day creating all living creatures on land and finally man. Man was made in God's image to represent and rule on his behalf. \nThe second narrative concentrate more on creation of human race. Though animals also made from dust; only man was given the breath of God. In order to give a help mate to Adam, the first woman was made out of Adam's rib. Adam named he; which shows his authority in marriage but they were made equal in tasks assigned to them.\nThus the Bible contains the most unique accounts of creation compared to any other document available.	9	2020-12-18 15:24:00+05:30	2021-01-09 20:20:00+05:30	\N	617	590
2283	The Bible evidently says man as a superior being above all other creatures. According to Genesis 1:27, it is a separate act of creation. After making man God said' very good' where as ' good' is used in relation to other creations. The superiority is vivid in genesis 2:7, where we see only Adam receiving the breath of God.\nThe superiority of man is evident in the fact that he is made in the image and likeness of God. man is also appointed to rule over the creation on behalf of God. God created humanity to reflect his glory and attribute. Man is given a superior role to administer God's rule over earth. Adam exercised this authority by naming all creatures. later the scripture confirms human superiority by putting him almost on the level of angels ( psalms 8:5).\nThough we see many people deny and destroy the distinction between human and animals; supporting evolution theory; we know that the humans are mentally superior to the animals. Humanity was created to be superior to the rest of creation in both dignity and authority.	9	2020-12-18 15:33:55+05:30	2021-01-09 20:20:00+05:30	\N	617	591
2284	India is a pluralistic society with different religious beliefs and cultures. The major religion Hinduism itself is pluralistic in relation to the myths on creation and origin of man. Though there are variations with different accounts, they have something common in them.\nHinduism believe creation as eternal and go through a process of creation and destruction. So beginning refers to the beginning of a phase. \nConcerning the origin of man, the major concept is Brahma created human and whole life. He created man of his soul. One of the stories mention that Brahma split in to two to create man and woman. According to the "Matsya purana', sage Manu was the first man created by Brahma. He was born through the union between Brahma and Shatrupa.( goddess). The rest of the race was born from the union of Manu and Ananti. \nRigveda has a different account of human origin which says human race was born from the five children ( Four male and one female)of lord prajapati; as Brahma was earlier called.\nHinduism also talk about cycle of rebirths. The theory evolution has a greater place in Hindu mythology of creation and human origin.\nThe biblical record of human origin is totally different from the Indian or Hindu concept. The union of god and goddess, process of evolution and cycle of rebirths are in contrast with the biblical concept of God making man in his own image and likeness.	0	2020-12-18 15:48:08+05:30	2020-12-18 15:48:08+05:30	\N	617	592
