2285	God made man with a purpose and entered in to a covenant relationship. garden of Eden as a sanctuary, a precursor to the Tabernacle or Temple; Adam and Eve had a priestly ministry to fulfill. As Adam and Eve were chosen to look after the garden, the old Testament priests were chosen to look after the tabernacle/ Temple. As priests represented God in the Temple; Adam and Eve represented God in the Garden of Eden. \nGod appointed Adam and Eve to rule over the creation on his behalf. The great King of heaven ordained humanity as his royal vassals to expand his Kingdom beyond the initial boarders his dwelling In the garden through multiplying and replenishing the whole earth. Ultimately the humanity was to turn the whole planet in to God's earthly sanctuary as an extension of his heavenly Kingdom. \nGod's covenant with Adam and Eve is binding to humanity. We are supposed to fulfill our priestly duty to serve God, worship him, cultivate and guard creation and to turn the whole world in to a sanctuary. Also we are supposed to exercise the divine authority given to us as the children of God. \nWe fulfill the priestly responsibility in the Church through rendering sacrifices of praise and Obedience obedient to him proclaiming his goodness. By preaching the gospel and manifesting the power of the Holy Spirit, we exercise the divine authority and establish the Kingdom of God. As we are supposed to represent and rule on behalf of God; in different capacity we represent God in life and spiritual disciplines and exercise divine authority in establishing the Kingdom of God on earth through establishing his Church. Thus both in life and ministry we fulfill the priestly and royal responsibility assigned to us.	9	2020-12-18 16:05:58+05:30	2021-01-09 20:20:00+05:30	\N	617	801
2291	As per the Westminster Shorter Catechism, \nSIN is any want of conformity or transgression against the law of God\nDisdain and complete disregard for God's law were central to humanity's first sin and they continue to characterize human race.\n\nWhen God created the first human race - Adam and EVe, they were sinless, they had no predisposition to sin and no reason to sin. God had given them authority to rule over other creatures that God had created. Clearly God had given them clear prohibition - they were forbidden to eat the fruit of the tree of the Knowledge of Good and Evil. There were 99% possibilities and probabilities to obey God and 1% prohibition to round it up to 100%. But unfortunately Adam and Eve fell for that 1% to round the negativity to 100%, leaving aside every other probability in obeying God - and hence disobeyed the very first covenant made with humanity represented through Adam and Eve. \n\nIn Genesis 3:1-7, the serpent tempted Eve to eat the forbidden fruit, and she gave some of it to Adam and he ate too. Immediately they realized they were naked and felt shame. that's the origin of sin in the human race. \n\nGod confronted Adam and Eve and cursed them because of their disloyalty. These events are summarized as The Fall of mankind, sin caused humanity to fall out of God's favor and blessings. \n\nAs a result of the fall, God judged man and women and indeed the whole of creation. Mankind experienced death because of the sin.\n\nAdam and Eve sinned and their sin was the origin of sin in the human race.	9	2020-12-24 21:29:06+05:30	2021-01-09 20:21:33+05:30	\N	618	791
2292	The idea of authorship of human sin is important since many opponents of Christianity have accursed God of authorizing humanity's fall into sin.\n\nAfter Adam and Eve ate the forbidden fruit, God judged the serpent, Adam and Eve. In the course of that judgement, Adam and Eve both tried to shift the blame to someone else. Adam was the first one to try to shift the blame to someone else. \n\nAdam blamed Eve, Eve blamed the serpent - \n\nAdam didn't deny eating the fruit, but he did attempt to avoid being held responsible. First he blamed his wife, who had givem him the fruit to eat. And second he blamed God, since God had created Eve. \n\nBoth Adam and Eve tried to arguie that the blame or authorship of their sin should be placed on someone else. And they tried achieving this to avoid punishment. But God didnt agree with their reasoning. \n\nAs far as God was concerned Adam and Eve were guilty as they chose to disobey his command.\n\nFrom scripture we can understand that the ultimate author of sin was the serpent, as it was the first character to come up with the idea to sin and first one to try to cause humanity to  sin. But Adam and Eve also contributed free choices to this event and in this sense authored human sin.\n\nBoth Adam and Eve knew God's command and freely chose to disobey him. There was no compulsion from any internal and external power. Their minds and choices were their own. In this way, humanity was culpable for their sin, and God was not.	8	2020-12-24 21:47:33+05:30	2021-01-09 20:21:33+05:30	\N	618	792
2293	Original sin refers to the consequences of humanity's first sin. Adam's disobedience negatively impacts every human being that naturally descends from him. \n\nOriginal sin, is sin that at bottom a person has possessed since he was born And a person cannot evade this sin. Every person who is born must accept this because people are born from a sinful lineage.\n\nWhen they sinned they lost ther sinless ability and retained only the ability to sin. The corruption they suffered removed their capacity to please God and to merit his blessings and left them only with the ability to sin.\n\nJesus and Paul compared this state of moral corruption to being slaves of sin. We all remain in this state of corruption until God saves us. \n\nJesus compared this corrupt state to a bad tree that can only produce bad fruit. He didn't mean that unsaved fallen humanity never does anything outwardly good. \n\nThe mind of sinful man is death, as their mind is hostile to God.\n\nFallen humanity, our corruption extends to every facet of human nature, every faculty of our human nature gets affected.\n\nThe 3 main areas werhein sin affects corruption\n\nCONCEPTS\nDue to sin both Adam and Eve's concepts were corrupted they disobeyed God and believed the lies of the serpent. But the most terrible thing about these corruption is that they were passed on to all human beings.\nSin has damaged humanity's capacity for conceptual thought and caused us to believe that false ideas are true. Sin has made us insane in many ways, we don't value what God and we commit ourselves to evil\n\nBEHAVIORS\nAdam and Eve's behavior was probably the most obvious aspect of their sin they ate the forbidden fruit. Humanity sinned and God has given us over to our sinful appetities.\nBehaviroal pattern was completely affected. Humanity was filled with every kind of wickedness and disobedience against God and with other humans.\n\nEMOTIONS :\nLove is an emotion that motivates us to bedience. Sinful corruption affects our emotions preventing us from loving God and our neighbors preventing us from ma	9	2020-12-24 22:07:36+05:30	2021-01-09 20:21:33+05:30	\N	618	793
2294	God told Adam that if he ate the fruit of the Tree of the knowledge of good and evil he would die. \n\nAfter the sin God cursed Adam to physical death. As covenant head of the entire human race, his rebellion against God affected our entire human race and fell under the shoadow of his guilt and consequently under the curse of death.\n\nPaul said that all sinned because God reckoned Adam's guilt not only to Adam, but to the rest of natural humanity too.\n\nAdam didn't die immediately when God cursed him, not physically though, but he died spiritually when he was cursed and his descendants are spiritually dead as well.\n\nPaul says in Ephesians that we are dead in our sins and our transgressions in which we used to live when you followed the ways of this world.\n\nAs natural descendants of Adam and Eve, the fallen nature was automatilly passed on to  the descendants - all the character of the fallen nature is manifested in all of humans which originated at the Fall of mankind. Human beings suffer immediate spiritual death. But worst if we never come to faith in Christ. If we are redeemed from sin's curse by God's grace, we will continue to suffer both spiritual and physical death. The curst of death and sin is very real.\n\nBut by God's grace we can over come sin's influence if we trust in the salvation that was appointed by God, by faith in the Lord Jesus Christ who will enable us to overcome all the sins and curses due to the fall of mankind.	8	2020-12-24 22:23:58+05:30	2021-01-09 20:21:33+05:30	\N	618	794
2295	When God created Adam and Eve he gave them the full liberty and choice either to obey God or to disobey Him. God who in his foreknowledge knew everything beforehand. But both Adam and Eve knoews God's command and freely chose to disobey him. There was no compulsion from any internal or external power. Their minds and choices were their own, in this way humanity as a whole was culpable for their sin. Sin was passed on to the descendants.\n\nSin crept into humanity through the disobedience of one man. Furthermore the fallen nature of mankind was evident in all facets of human nature. Violenece, wickedness and self interest preceded over all other relationships, resulting in pain, sorrow and death Sin took the precedence over everything else and damaged man's relationship with God and also reflecting in the behavior pattern with the rest of the humans.\n\nThough God is love, yet God gave mankind the free choice or will power to chose their paths whether in obedience or disobedience, thereby going through the consequence of sin and pain and death.\n\nBut inspite of all the curses and disobedience God's love was evident in Genesis 3:15 wherein God also promised a future redemption for all of mankind. \n\nThere was a ray of hope for all humans to go through the plan of salvation that God himself had authorized.\n\nThough our God is a loving God, yet he allows all humans to go through a process. God allows us to learn through our mistakes and in the process have faith not in our own abilities but to blindly trust in God's path of salvation and beliefs. \n\nAll humans have to go through this life cycle, where the main turning poing it whether to Obey God or Disobey God - accordingly we will meet our destiny. \n\nOur choices and decisions determine our destiny in life. If we are willing to be governed by a loving God or whether we choose to rebel against God and his will,\n\nBut in all these processes of life that we go through all have sinned and fall short of the glor