2301	The office of the image of God is rooted in the authority God gave to humanity to rule over his creation on his behalf.( genesis 1:27-28). So we hold the office of delegated ruler. In theological terms we are God's vassal regents - his administrative deputies or in ancient near eastern terms, his servant or vassal kings. \nHuman beings are physical representatives that remind all creation of God's power, authority and goodness. And through us, he manifest his rule over the world and all its creatures.\nThe nature of our role is first introduced in Genesis 1: 27-28. " Be fruitful and increase in number; fill the earth and subdue it. Rule over the fish of the sea and the birds of the air and over every living creatures that moves on the ground. Just after the creation of man, God commanded his office and explained the nature of his role on the earth.	7	2021-01-08 15:08:53+05:30	2021-01-09 20:22:36+05:30	\N	622	786
2302	The first thing scripture tells about humanity is that we are the image and likeness of God. The term likeness further defines that we are not exact copies of God. So it is a representational dynamic, not a static copy of him. \nThe Hebrew words for Image and likeness are not identical. Image can be a curved or cast idol. By contrast likeness never represent an idol. It describes the appearance or sound of one thing by comparing it to another. \nAlthough not identical, the meaning of image and likeness overlap because they both describe a model or sketch of a greater reality. In a similar way human beings are images and likeness of God because we model God's power, authority and goodness. Many theologians argue that collective meaning while image points to our similarity with God, Likeness distinguishes between God and humanity, to avoid wrong assumption that we are exactly like God. \nOur office as the image of God elevates all humanity to the level of royalty; with a task of administering God's reign on earth. This gives us great dignity, but still under divine authority.	8	2021-01-08 15:19:37+05:30	2021-01-09 20:22:36+05:30	\N	622	787
2303	It is understood that image of God included the capacity to think rationally. Man used his rationale to give appropriate names to the animals in Genesis 2:19-20. Some of these rational abilities we lost by fall, as evidenced in many biblical passages that speak human of being irrational and insane at times. According to Deuteronomy 29: 2-3, the mind of Israel could not understand the significance of the miracles of God performed for them. In John 8, Jesus referred the unbelievers as the children of the devil who is the father of lies. As a result they believe lies and are incapable of accepting the truth. "The gentiles live in futility of their thinking. They are darkened in their understanding and separated from the life of God because of the ignorance that  is in them due to the hardening of their hearts. ( Ephesians".  (4:17-18)\nOur fall in to sin damaged our ability to think and to understand the world from God's perspective; though it was not destroyed completely.  Paul told in Colossians that the restoration of our rational abilities is an aspect of the image of God being renewed in us. \nThrough Christ God begins to restore the lost image of God in man by which we are able to think and understand more correctly, so that, our thought and reason become more aligned with his.	8	2021-01-08 15:32:32+05:30	2021-01-09 20:22:36+05:30	\N	622	788
2304	The three aspects of covenant relationship with God are : 1. Our obligation to reflect God's Character. 2. Our duty to promote pure worship. 3. Our responsibility to build God's Kingdom. \nMan is supposed to reflect the pure, holy and righteous character of God. 1 Peter 1:15-16. Ass fallen man fell short of reflecting God's character; we rely entirely on Christ's perfect holiness for our standing before God. \nAny form of false worship especially of idol is prohibited in scriptures. Moses reminded that God had not revealed himself in a physical form to protect the purity of worship. He wanted Israel's relationship with God pure through worship, unadulterated by the idolatrous theology and practice of the surrounding nations. \nWhen God commanded to fill the earth, he was instructing us to place the images of himself every where through out the world and demonstrate God's rule every where they go. The scripture says fallen human beings as against God's kingdom and belongs to the enemy Satan's Kingdom ( Ephesians 2: 1-2). Until we come to the faith in the Lord Jesus Christ, we continue to struggle against God's Kingdom. Nevertheless, all human beings are tasked with building God's Kingdom especially the spiritual kingdom in the New Testament perspective.	8	2021-01-08 15:45:48+05:30	2021-01-09 20:22:36+05:30	\N	622	789
2321	Hermeneutics is a common word in theological  and biblical studies. the word hermeneutics derives from the family of Greek terms , the name, the  ' hermes' the mythological messenger of the god. the family of Greek words related to the hermeneu, which means  interpret or explain. when we refer to hermeneutics we have in mind the interpretation or explanation of some kind of message or communication. biblical hermeneutics is the study of interpreting the meaning and the significance of the scripture. when we read the scripture , then we are involved ourselves in hermeneutics at least informally. informal approaches to the bible are of great value , and these lessons will build on what most of us already understand. one particular aspect of biblical hermeneutics is that we try to see to relate all the data of scripture together under the assumption that they don't contradict one another, but rather they speak - while of the variety of God's revelation, they also speak one in agreement with itself.	8	2021-01-12 23:12:20+05:30	2021-02-03 03:04:39+05:30	\N	624	675
2305	As the image of God, man was created to protect,  felicitate and  rule the world and all the creation on his behalf. But man lost his image and accordingly his authority and failed to fulfill his responsibility  towards God and the creation. but God in his mercy reinstated man to relationship with him. But in Christ Jesus and through the Covenant of grace only man is perfectly restored to perfect relationship with God to fulfill God given responsibilities. \nAs  ministers of the New Testament, primarily we are entitled to represent God or Jesus Christ in reflecting our Character to the world. In a lost world of sin and Chaos; We are appointed as light in the darkness. \nSecondly we are supposed to maintain true worship of God according to the scriptures. It's our responsibility to convince the world of their futile ways of false worship and lead them to the true worship and right relationship with God .\nAnd ultimately our responsibility is to expand the Kingdom of God through the preaching of the gospel of Jesus Christ. The devil's Kingdom is defeated and Christ's Kingdom is established through turning people from their wicked ways and to the saving knowledge of Jesus Christ. We use God given authority and the power of the Holy Spirit to establish God's Kingdom, His Church. \nIn my ministry I try to reflect God's character, to establish true worship and to establish God's Kingdom through preaching the gospel by using the divine authority vested on me.	8	2021-01-08 16:03:51+05:30	2021-01-09 20:22:36+05:30	\N	622	790
