2308	In traditional systematic theology, the term 'original sin' refers to the consequences of humanity's first sin.  It is the condition in which Adam's natural descendants are born as a result of Adam's fall in to sin. \nMan lost his original ability not to sin by fall. The corruption Adam and Eve suffered removed their capacity to please God and to merit his blessings. They were left with only the ability to sin and merit God's curse. \nBy means of faith and repentance God restored their ability to avoid sin but unfortunately this was not extended to the descendants. The generation were born with the moral corruption to being slaves to sin. \nSin is pervasive in our lives. It corrupts every part of humanity's being- Body, soul, minds, desires, thoughts and everything else. And as a result also it corrupts everything that flows from our being - everything we think, do and feel. When we come to the faith in Christ, god renew us in ways that restore our ability to please him in all these areas. \nSin has damaged human capacity for conceptional thought, and caused us to believe that false ideas are true. we don't value what God value and we commit ourselves to evil Ephesians 4:17-18.\nAdam's sin served as the model for all the behavioral sins that have plagued humanity since then. This sinful behavior caused God to destroy the entire human race with a flood. Romans 1:29-32.\nThe sinful corruption also affect our emotions, preventing us from loving God and our neighbors as we should . Also it prevents us from manifesting other righteous emotions that flow from this love. This affected the social and family relations as well. Pervasive corruption is one of the terrible consequence of man's fall.	9	2021-01-11 15:38:44+05:30	2021-01-11 22:44:14+05:30	\N	625	793
