2340	God the Son (Christ) the second person of the Trinity, joined the covenant as its mediator. As a mediator the Son intercedes for Gods covenant people.  He reconciles us to God by taking both the blame and the punishment for our sins. He preserves the integrity of the covenant and the lives of the people by suffering the covenant curses on our behalf.\n\nThrough his obedience to the covenant's requirement of human loyalty the Son earns the covenant blessings and then shares them with the sinners he redeems.\n\nChrist began to mediate the covenant of grace when it was first made back in the garden of Eden, when God first offered redemption to Adam and Eve. Ad he's continued to mediate ever since. No one was ever saved on the basis of his or her own merit, since no works of obedience can erase our sin. \n\nNo one was ever saved on the basis of sacrificed animals, since it would not be sufficient substitute for a human being.\n\nThe Son's mediation of the covenant of grace centered around his incarnation, life of perfect faith and obedience, his death on the cross and his resurrection from the dead, his ascention into heaven. As mediator of the covenant of grace, he fulfilled the covenant works on our behalf and guaranteed that we would receive its blessings.\n\nAdam's sin had thrown the entire human race under the curse of sin and death. But the Son's role as a mediator fulfilled both covenants, the covenant of works and the covenant of grace.\n\nAdam's history revolved around sin, failure, condemnation and death. All humanity was condemned in Adam. It did not provide a mechanism for mercy and forgiveness. it did not provide a mediator. There was nothing that could do within the covenant of works to reverse our condemnation.\n\nJesus succeeded where Adam had failed Jesus righteous works benefited us because the covenant of grace does provide mechanism for mercy and forgiveness. Jesus history centers on obedience, righteousness, justification and life.	9	2021-01-14 22:51:11+05:30	2021-02-03 03:06:19+05:30	\N	626	799
2341	The covenant of grace was governed or administered by various covenant representatives. Considering the historical administration of the covenant of grace it is important to recognize that different theological traditions define these administration in different ways.\n\nAdamic Administration\nAdam representated the covenant head of all humanity, its also known as Adamic administration of the covenant. This administratio provided human beings with immediate opportunity to reconcile our relationships with God. This goal is evident not only through God's refusal to destroy mankind, but also in the subsequent account of Adam's faithful descendants. The descendants of Adam, began to call on the name of the Lord, shows that they were determined to fulfill the covenant obligation to God\n\nNoah Administration\nThe covenant with Noah was confirmed after the flood. It expanded the covenant blessings also incorporating Adamic covenant. God promised to never aain destroy the earth with flood waters and also provided a rainbow as sign to this covenant. God also reaffirmed his kingdom purposes for humanity by giving Noah and his family the same command to be fruitful and increase in number to fill the earth, the same command he gave to Adam and EVe.\n\nAbrahamic Administration\nAbrahamic covenant administration included the terms from Noahic administration. God promised Abraham to turn his descendants into a might namtion and to bless all nations through them especially the nation of Israel\n\nMoses \nMosaic administraation is provided in great detail throughtout the books of Leviticus and Deuteronomy.  Not only did God build on the Abrahamic administration but also provided structure for the nation of Israel as a nation by providing them codified version of the law.\n\nDavid :\nDavidic administration is described in the book of Samuel and in Psalms\nGod confirmed the Mosaic administration but also revealed the greatest covenant blessing that would be fulfilled under the kingship of David and his dynastic heirs\n\n\nJesus\nThe final covenant representative, the administration is referred to as The New Covenant. This name originally comes from the book	9	2021-01-14 23:11:14+05:30	2021-02-03 03:06:19+05:30	\N	626	800
