2392	Biblical elaborations are places where one part of scripture directly or indirectly comments on an aspect of the meaning of another passage in scripture. sometimes an elaboration is stated as a repetition of a facet of the original meaning . \nat other times , a biblical elaboration may be stated as a clarification of things that they weren't entirely apparent or well understood. at other times , a biblical elaboration can be expansion of the meaning of a  particular passage\n you shall not murder Exodus 20:13\nthe first biblical elaboration mentioned is primarily a repetition of these exact words in Deuteronomy 5:17\n the second type of elaboration we listed was clarification and we find it in Numbers 35:20-25\nthe third type of biblical elaboration is expansion  ,in which scripture provide additional information about the passage or topic: Mathew5:21-22\nAccording to Jesus elaboration , unrighteous anger violates the same principle that murder does. Anger is not as bas as murder, but it offends the same aspect of God's character.\nJesus invites us to go back to the principles behind exodus that its not just enough not to commit the sin , but we should not want to commit the sin, That is Jesus is not only is interested in our behavior but in our character, not just on what we do, but in who we are.	9	2021-02-02 23:33:25+05:30	2021-02-03 03:17:08+05:30	\N	635	688
