2399	Many modern Christians without denying the value and importance of scientific research, continued to hold that the scripture are true in all that they claim, including history. \nModern Evangelical Theologian Charles Hodge defined biblical theology as an exegetical discipline, the study of the facts of scripture. And also he defined systematic theology as the discipline that takes the facts discerned in biblical theology and arranges them in relation to each other. In contrast with the critical theologians, Hodge believed in the authority of the scripture. He taught that Christians are obligated to base systematic theology on the findings of the biblical theology. Followed by Benjamin B Warfield, it was explained that the teachings of scripture were already logically organized in the Bible itself. \nHe argued that the Bible never contradicts itself; all of its teachings are harmonious; though the authors described theology in different perspective and style. Thus they described systematic theology as an effort to bring all the theologies of the Bible in to a unified system. \nGeerhardus Vos agreeing to Hodge and Warfield, went further to say that the various theologies of the scripture had a common focus on the history of redemption. \nThe efforts of such theologians to establish the authenticity of biblical theology and the initiative to connect with systematic theology harmoniously has caused modern Christians to approach scriptures through biblical theology.	8	2021-02-03 15:44:55+05:30	2021-03-10 21:27:02+05:30	\N	638	658
