2489	Christian faith affirms that there is only one God, and that this God exists in three persons, namely the person of the father, the son and the Holy Spirit. The mention of these three name together and on equal terms implies that while the father, the son and the Holy Spirit are all distinct persons, they are only one God. Apostles' creed does not mention the term 'Trinity' or spell out its details, but people understood God as one and in three persons. \nThe Trinity is commonly stated this way: God has three persons, but only one essence. By the term 'person' we mean a distinct, self aware personality. And by the term ' essence' we are referring to God's fundamental nature of the substance of which he consists. \nRegarding father, the creed ascribes to him the attribute of being Almighty, the maker of heaven and earth. The creed describes more about the earthly life and ministry of Jesus Christ; The incarnation, life, suffering, death, burial, resurrection, ascension in to heaven and finally his role as a judge.\n Of the Holy Spirit , the creed says the he caused the virgin Mary to become pregnant with Jesus. The creed also associates the Holy spirit with the Church, and with our experience of salvation both now and in future.	9	2021-03-15 15:36:04+05:30	2021-05-11 04:27:07+05:30	\N	655	868
