2509	The word 'ontological' means ' relating to being'.  So we look at the Trinity in terms of being and essence in it; how the three persons of the Trinity are integrated with one another, and how they are single in essence. \nFrom the perspective of ontology, all three persons of God interact with each other, how they relate to one another as individual persons. In this view, each persons has different responsibilities, a different level of authority and a different assigned role with different task to perform. \nThe father, son and the Holy Spirit engage in conversation with each other, make agreements with each other, and interact in many other ways. Both ontological and economic perspectives, the father is said to be the first person of the Trinity. In ontological perspective the Son is said to be generated by the father, and the Holy Spirit said to proceed from the father. From the Economic perspective, the father is said to be the first person because he has the authority over the other two persons.	8	2021-03-17 15:28:17+05:30	2021-05-11 04:25:35+05:30	\N	661	873
