2546	While studying the book of Hebrews - the five important factors or characteristics of the original audience for whom the book is addressed is as follows :\n\n1) Jewish \nMajority of the original audience was Jewish Hebrews.\n\nAs mentioned in Hebrews 1:1 \nIn the past God spoke to our forefathers through the propohets and in various ways. \n\nHere the author refers to the Old Testament Israelites as "our forefathers" as the ancestors of the author and his audience.\n\n2) Hellenistic :\nA large part of the originial audience were Hellenistic. The familiarity of the audience with the teachings that were common to Jews living outside of Palestine as referred to in Hebrews 13:24 wherein it mentions, "those from Italy"\n\n3) Immature \nThe original audience of Hebrews were referred to as immature. As they have been believers for a long time but they could not make further progress in their beliefs and faith. The author notes that they need to be taught the elementary truths about God all over again as mentioned in Hebrews 5:12\n\n4) Persecuted\nThe original audience were under persecution. The Roman rulers - emperors persecuted the Christians for their beliefs. They already faced persecution in the past and it was an ongoing process of suffering in the present and the possiblity of future persecution, with the severity increasing. \n\nHebrews 10:32-35 - exhorts the believers to not throw away your confidence since it will be richly rewarded.\n\n5) Near Apostasy.\nDue to the severity of the persecutions many of the believers were are the brink of embracing apostasy turning away from Christ entirely.\n\nThe author of Hebrews warned such category of believers, warining them not to turn away from Christ., wherein no sacrifice for sins is left.	8	2021-04-23 21:07:37+05:30	2021-05-11 04:28:33+05:30	\N	666	777
2547	The author of Hebrews wrote to exhort his audience. Exhortation implies to summon the speakers side or to take the speaker's point of view.\n\nThe frequency of the exhortation co-relates to the urgency of the messages. These messages were implicit at times and at least 30 times they appear explicitly.\n\nTo urge - to implore, encouraging - exhorting the audience to do this or that. using imperatives, direct orders, associated with persuasive oratory.\n\nThe book of Hebrews has been characterized as highly rhetorical, can be categorized as follows \n\n1) Rhetorical devise called synkrisis in Greek - comparison between 2 or more things to convince the audience to affirm the speaker's point of view.\n\n2) Another rhetorical devise of Exempla, list of illustrations or examples that follow one another to build a reasonable argument to prove a point.\n\n3) The third rhetorical devise - Expression - gol wahomer - can be translated as light to heavy. Such arguments begin with simple explanation graduating to more complex conclusion. \n\nThese examples help us to see the urgency of the author's intentions using different rhetoric styles to convince the audience.	8	2021-04-23 21:23:48+05:30	2021-05-11 04:28:33+05:30	\N	666	778
2548	The original audience of Hebrews were immature. \nHebrews 5:12 Though by this time you ought to be teachers, you need someone to teach you the truths all over again.\n\nThey have been belieers for over a long time, and they should have made doctrinal progress. But the author finds out that they need to be taught all over again starting from the elementary truths of God's word.\n\nIn other words they are unable to grow in the doctrine that they have learned, the very reason may be that they are unable to apply the basic truths and the doctrine in their personal life. Since the more you learn spiritual truths, you should be able to apply it to your practical life and automatically God would enable you to grow in the Word.\n\nSince they have been believers over a long period of time but they have faltered somewhere in their lives, hence they need to be taught all over again.\n\nAs parents we should be able to explain our faith and beliefs to our children, as neightbors to our friends and people staying around us. \n\nBelievers over a stronger period of time, but no growth factor. Dull of hearing and not able to apply the teachings to their personal life.\n\nAs a person, my individual faith life also needs to grow in the grace of God. The more we learn about the doctrinal truths, combining with faith when we apply it to our individual lives, God does the rest by helping us to grow. Studying the word and praying for God's providence and grace is the way forward to enhance one's personal faith in God.	9	2021-04-23 21:43:02+05:30	2021-05-11 04:28:33+05:30	\N	666	779
