2964	Jesus' experiences prove that he was truly human by a few different factors. To begin, Jesus was conceived through human birth. Although Mary was a virgin and she and Joseph did not have physical relations leading to the birth of Jesus, He was conceived by the Holy Spirit and born to a female. He began as a baby in his mother's worm and was formed in the same form and fashion as every other baby is molded in a mother's womb. He did not descend from heaven as a supernatural being, rather was brought into this world through his mother's womb as a human being. The next point to note is that Jesus was a real person, a real man with a physical human body. He offered his physical being to be punished, humiliated and tortured for divine judgement to atone for the sins of humankind. \n\nIt can be a common belief for people to accept that a god could disguise himself as a human being, but that is not what Jesus did here. He actually became a human being and went through the physical and emotional parts of a human being. Which then brings us to the point of his physical form, Jesus was arrested and crucified after being flogged, spit on, forced to wear a crown of thorns. His body was one that was beaten, bruised and bled. A body that at one point from exhaustion, collapsed, and was buried in a tomb and allowed for his soul to depart. When Jesus was on the cross, he committed his spirit into the hands of the Father. We can see that when Jesus died, his physical body was buried by men, but his spirit was committed into the hands of God, the Father. When our bodies die as humans, our souls are separated from our bodies and continue in a conscious state.	8	2023-06-19 18:01:03+05:30	2023-07-04 01:03:43+05:30	\N	808	878
