3012	Apostles Creed is a statement of Christian belief that is used by churches both Catholic and Protestant. It reflects traditions that were affirmed officially by the entire church. Although its roots are much earlier, in its present form it dates to about eighth century.    The earliest  written from this creed is found in a letter that Ancyra wrote in Greek to Julius, the bishop of Rome. About 50 years later, Tyrannius Rufinus wrote a commentary on this creed in Latin. In it, he recounted the view point that apostles wrote the creed together after Pentecost, before leaving to Jerusalem to preach. The title "Apostles" Creed is also mentioned about 390 by Ambrose, where he refers to the "the creed of the Apostles which the Church of Rome keeps an guard in its entirety.  Whatever we now know as the Apostles creed is an enlargement of the Old Roman Creed. Over the next few centuries, the Apostles Creed in its final form gained acceptance through out France and Germany. The Creed as it exists today consists of three main articles, like the Old Roman Creed divided according to a Trinitarian arrangement. The apostles Creed seems to represent some form of what the early church called the rule of faith.	8	2023-10-18 07:45:32+05:30	2023-11-08 15:26:30+05:30	\N	836	866
