3129	While Paul was imprisoned, he suffered quite a bit, to the point that he felt that death would be his only escape. However by overcoming all of these challenges, he continued to persevere and later exhorted to the Philippians to persevere. He instructed them to continue to remain faithful to Christ no matter what and to live their lives exemplary even during difficult times in their lives. \n\nThe types of exhortations Paul provided can be categorized into four main topics, the first being the importance of perseverance, the help that ministers provide, Paul's personal example, and the challenges to persevere. No matter how difficult the challenges were that the Philippians faced, nothing was beyond God's control. God had actually planned their suffering as a means of blessing for them. That is why it was so important for them to understand that. Paul did not want them to simply undergo this suffering, he wanted them to rejoice in the midst of it. and he continue to persevere by sending ministers to help care for them. \n\nDespite the hardships that Paul faced, he used himself as a positive example of perseverance in faith, behavior and mindset. Paul mentioned that purely professing faith alone is not enough to guarantee salvation, you must also persevere in faith in order to obtain eternal life. Paul stressed the importance of living holy lives, maintaining ones faith. If one is not able to persevere, then we prove that our faith was false to begin with and not genuine.	9	2024-02-20 07:36:04+05:30	2024-03-03 11:10:19+05:30	\N	860	924
