3134	The threefold criteria for good works can be outlined by proper motive, proper standard, and proper goal. With proper motive, you are driven by a heart that is purified by faith. Without seeking God's blessing founded on basis of faith, we are not able to please God. Love is the next step of proper motive, everything that we do should be stemmed around the basis of love. \n\nWith proper standard, every work that is done must adhere to the standard of God's work and his commandments. When referring to commands, there are no commands that can be bypassed or omitted, each command of God still holds true to be upheld. All scripture is basis for commands and law, and there is good reason for scripture to be used for ethical training. \n\nLastly, proper goal is when the ultimate goal should always be considered. God's glory is to be a central, and foundational goal in our lives and God only rewards and approves the work of those that have his glory as their ultimate goal.	7	2024-02-21 07:24:40+05:30	2024-03-03 11:09:39+05:30	\N	861	828
3135	When looking at the different perspective that must be employed when approaching ethics, the first is situational. This approach can be referred to as 'teleological' because of the focus on the end result or action. In scripture we can see how Paul would encourage his readers to live a holy life and abstain from sin that they had once committed. This situational perspective creates awareness for the sake of righteousness and leads towards the reward that is mentioned for demonstrating situational perspective. \n\nNormative perspective is the fact that God's word is the norm or the basis of ethical standards. When considering normative perspective, you are looking to the Bible in order to be told what is the correct thing to do. This is the basis for behavior and the commandment for how people should behave in a certain way. \n\nLastly, is existential which is viewing ethics through the lens of the individual's personal experience. The Scripture affirms the leading of the Holy Spirit as a valid means to determining what is right and wrong, and God moves among his people to bring them towards conviction on a personal level. When we acknowledge this, we are using existential perspective.	9	2024-02-21 07:31:10+05:30	2024-03-03 11:09:39+05:30	\N	861	829
