3164	Hermeneutics is an effort to interpret the meaning of communication, particularly communication that is being interpreted in a different cultural context. Biblical hermeneutics is the method of interpreting Scriptures so we can bridge the gaps between modern-day readers of the Bible, it's original audiences, and God as its ultimate author. \nHermeneutics is foundation to the theological study, whether or not they know it, every biblical reader interprets the Bible through their own hermeneutics. Developing a clearly communicated biblical hermeneutics helps Bible students to understand the biases they bring into their interpretive work. without effective methods of interpretation, we can't understand the meaning of the text and therefore build cohesive biblical theologies, and therefore, a Christ-honoring, mission-driven Christian life. \n\nThe church today faces many important issues as technological innovation transforms everything from communications to family structures to social relationships. We need the wisdom form God himself to properly engage and  understand the world we live in.  Yet the primary way we learn what God has to say is the Bible , a book written between 2,000 to 3,500 years ago.  \n\nTheological interpretation of scriptures is an approach to biblical interpretation that approaches the text with explicitly theological presuppositions, questions, and concerns. seeking to hear in scriptures not only thoughts and voices human authors but a word from God that functions as the primary.	8	2024-03-11 07:46:31+05:30	2024-03-20 20:38:58+05:30	\N	869	681
