3167	The three most prominent theories of knowledge are:\n1. Foundationalism: Foundationalism is the view that all knowledge is based on a foundation of self-evident or indubitable beliefs. These foundational beliefs are then used to justify all other beliefs.\n\n2. Coherentism: Coherentism is the view  that all knowledge is justified by its coherence with other beliefs. In other words, a belief is justified if it is a part of coherent system of beliefs. \n\n3. Reliabilism: Reliabilism is the view that all knowledge is justified if it is produced by a reliable process. In other words, a belief is justified if it is produced by a process that is likely to lead to true beliefs. \n\nThese three theories of knowledge has its own strength and weakness. Foundationalism is appealing because it seems to provide a solid foundation for our knowledge. However, it is difficult to identify any self-evident or indubitable beliefs. Coherentism is appealing because it allows us to justify beliefs that are not directly based on experience.  However, it's difficult to say how coherent a system of beliefs must be in order to be justified. Reliabilism is appealing because it seems to focus on what is important in practice. \n\nUltimately, none of these theories of knowledge is perfect. However they provide us with different ways of thinking about what justifies our beliefs.	8	2024-03-11 08:29:15+05:30	2024-03-20 20:38:58+05:30	\N	869	684
3168	Whether we are aware of it or not, we always bring certain beliefs and philosophical assumptions to our research. Sometimes these are deeply ingrained views about the types of problems that we need to study. what research questions to ask, or how we go about gathering data. These beliefs are instilled in us during our educational training through reading journal articles and books.\nThe difficulty lies first in becoming aware of these assumptions and believes and second in deciding whether we will actively incorporate them in our qualitative studies. Often, at a less abstract level, these philosophical assumptions inform our choice of theories that guide our research.\nTheories are more apparent in our qualitative studies than philosophical assumptions and theories are made explicit for us in our scholarly training and in report research studies. \n\nQualitative researchers have underscored the importance of not only understanding the beliefs and theories that inform our research but also actively writing about them in our reports and studies. \n\nA close tie does exist between the philosophy that one brings to the research act and hour one proceeds to use a framework to shroud his or he inquiry. Further, various interpretive frameworks are suggested that link back to philosophical assumptions.	8	2024-03-11 08:44:26+05:30	2024-03-20 20:38:58+05:30	\N	869	685
3169	There are many different types of subjectivism. But in general, we can say that subjectivist recognize that human beings and the world, and especially matters of faith, are often too complex to be discerned by scientific rationalism. So their search for typically relief strongly on personal faculties like intuition and emotions. For example in John 13:34-35, Jesus gave this familiar instruction:\n\nA new command I give you: Love one another . As I have loved , so you must love one another. By this all men will know that you are my disciples. if you love one another.\n\nSubjective approaches to meaning shifted again in the late twentieth century in a movement known as post-structuralism. In our days, subjectivism has become widespread , especially in the interpretation of art and literature. Subjective interpreters argue that since we can't discover the objective understanding of the world around us.\n\nIdeally, followers of Christ do not allow the currents of culture surrounding them to influence the way they interpret the Bible. But, in reality, none of us can entirely escape the effects of culture on our approach to biblical hermenutics. In recent recades, hermeneutical subjectivism  has moved beyond the confines of academic discusssions.	8	2024-03-11 09:01:44+05:30	2024-03-20 20:38:58+05:30	\N	869	686
