3213	I personally find a high level of confidence in knowing that scholars today have access to many manuscripts that contain the original words of Scripture. Biblical passages can be complicated and the original intentions of the authors may at times be multifaceted. While considering the genre considerations as well, things tend to be more complicated as well. This can create several intracacies of the original meaning of the Scripture, and can then require Christians to have a complex approach when considering the meaning of Scripture. \nWhile there is a high level of confidence in knowing that scholars have the access to many manuscripts which contain the original words of Scripture, the greatest defeat that must be considered is that while God had spoken his inspired Word to come to life, the iterations and translations and interpretations are still being done by humans. That is where there is still room for error to be made, motives to be different and where one person can decide how the word should be interpreted. This can then create vague limitations and boundaries of the biblical passage and meanings, and the translation can vary from one person to another.	9	2024-06-28 18:33:50+05:30	2024-11-21 02:04:06+05:30	\N	877	683
3214	Three major approaches towards the objects and subjects of knowledge are objective, subjective, and dialogical. When considering objective approaches, scholars believe that they can impartially interpret the Scripture. With background and influence, this is achieved by scholars in obtaining an exhaustive understanding of everything that they have studied. There are both philisophical and cultural backgrounds to consider with this approach of knowledge. \nThe second approach is that of subjective which is where subjectivists acknowledge human beings, the world, and matters of faith are often too complex to be discerned by scientific rationalization. Therefore many of their search for answers are relied upon heavily with emotions and intuition. For example, when Jesus said that we must love one another, there was an authoritative command with that. However as human beings, this is taken into consideration according to the weakness of mankind with emotion and intuition. \nLastly, the dialogical approach is where dialog and discussion is required between the reader and the text. The Psalmist refers to this when they talk about spending time in the word and meditating on it day and night, this requires that a reader be able to spend time with the text and have an open dialogue to understand the context and the meaning with that Scripture.	9	2024-06-28 18:46:13+05:30	2024-11-21 02:04:06+05:30	\N	877	684
