3198	There are many epochal or significant developments that have occurred over the course of redemptive history that have made our world different from the world of the Bible. For example the perspective laid out in the Bible is separated by three stages. The first being Creation, when God first made the world. The second being the Fall, when mankind fell into the temptation of sin and when sin was first committed and mankind was cursed. The last being redemption, when God showed His mercy and redeemed us from our sin. One example of how epochal developments occurred within history can be traced back to the laws regarding atoning sacrifices and how they required different things at different points in history. For example, during the time of Moses, they required sacrifices at the tabernacle, and then during the days of Solomon, they required sacrifices at the temple. In the early days of the New Testament, the required Jesus to be hung to death on a cross, and then later on in the New Testament, they ceased to be offered altogether. There have been many cultural developments between the original and modern audiences as well that must be taken into consideration, along with personal developments that distinguish people today from the audiences of the Bible.	8	2024-06-15 08:52:53+05:30	2024-06-19 05:17:14+05:30	\N	879	694
