3208	The general resurrection will have an impact and effect on creation three different ways. It will impact the natural world, hell, and heaven. In regards to how the general resurrection will impact the natural world, God will uses events in the end time to alter how the natural world operates in order to prepare for his presence. When mankind fell into the trap of sin, the curse of God was placed upon us and it became a place of danger and death. However, in Romans 8, Paul looked forward to the general resurrection as a solution to this curse/problem. With the general resurrection, the Earth would be rescued through the resurrection of redeemed humanity. With this redemption, creation itself will be liberated. \n\nThe impact on hell will be that when the unregenerate are resurrected, their souls will be removed from hell and then they will have their bodies returned to earth so that they can face God's judgement. However this won't just apply to the unregenerate, Satan and the demons in hell will be emptied from hell. According to some theologians, Revelation 20 teaches that Satan and demos will be released from their imprisonment in hell to participate in a final rebellion against God. \n\nThe impact on heaven is that heaven will no longer be the residence of regenerate souls as a result of the general resurrection. While heaven is a wonder place, the intention of God was never for us to live there forever. God has something even better for us in mind in the new heavens and earth. The resurrected regenerate will return to earth in order to appear before God's judgement throne. Heaven will be emptied of it's angels and when Jesus returns, he will bring all of his angels with him and they will collect the resurrected regenerate  according to Matthew 24:31.	8	2024-06-28 07:22:29+05:30	2024-11-21 02:03:27+05:30	\N	881	650
