3222	God is three persons in one essence, meaning that there is one substance in three persons. Our belief is that there is only one God, not three Gods. There are three persons within this one God, the Father, the Son, and the Holy Spirit. The Father is the one who sends the Son and the Holy Spirit. Think of God as being the Father figure, the Father sends the Son to the Earth, and once the Son dies and is resurrected, He goes to the Father. At that time, they send the Holy Spirit. \n\nBeing able to understand this also requires the understanding that God is one divine essence. He was never created, He was the Creator. He is the one who created the universe and all of the orders within. Many times we try to think of God as three different individuals, however they are the same essence, but with three different roles and responsibilities. The Father can not replace the Son, and the Son cannot replace the Father. Likewise the Holy Spirit can not replace the Father and vice versa. The three in one has a distinct meaning in that God has provided a clear distinction for each role of the Triune concept to understand the real meaning of Trinity.	9	2024-08-05 06:45:34+05:30	2024-08-14 09:34:55+05:30	\N	882	927
3223	In respect to the Trinity, a person is the distinction given to the roles of Father, Son and Holy Spirit. One thing to be clear on is that we do not mean the modern concept of an individual focused on the concept of personality. Looking at the New Testament, we can see passages of how the Father, Son and Holy Spirit speak to one another about each other. They love one another in some way that suggests the notion of communication amongst each other. While there remains one substance, you have three persons in that one substance. The persons do not have their own individual essence, rather they abide within one divine essence. \n\nA great example of this is displayed during the baptism of Jesus Christ by John the Disciple. When Jesus had emerged from the water, there was a sound from heaven, declaring the favor of God upon His Son in whom He was well pleased. That is the distinct person of the Father speaking directly to His Son. Then we see the example of the Holy Spirit in the form of a dove coming into the scene. This is the person of the Holy Spirit within the realm of the Triuness of God. There is one essential essence, but three persons.	7	2024-08-05 06:54:04+05:30	2024-08-14 09:34:55+05:30	\N	882	928
