3224	The reason that God's divine threeness does not violate the doctrine of God's essence is because you can not divide God into three different people. It is tricky, because people tend to confuse Trinity with tritheism, and what it makes it more difficult is that man cannot analyze him and figure this out for themselves. Theology shows us the 'simplicity' of God, and an analogy that has been used many times to describe the essence of God is related to water. With water, you can have different forms of one essence, for example when water is at normal temperature, it take the form of liquid. Under cold temperature, the water turns hard and into ice, but still remains under the essence of water. Lastly when water is boiled and heated to a certain degree, it can cause steam and evaporation which is still an essence of water. The Father will always remain the Father of His Son. His Son will always remain the Son of His Father, and that goes back to forever in time. The Holy Spirit has always been there, and the three of them are inseparable. \n\nIn the book of Matthew, we see of Jesus talking about how if anyone regardless of who, receives 'one of my disciples in my name, they receive the One who sent me.' When you receive the disciples that were sent by the God, and has the Spirit of God in them, then you are receiving God, the Father, and the Son and the Holy Spirit. God is one but three persons that are of one divine essence.	8	2024-08-05 07:03:28+05:30	2024-08-14 09:34:55+05:30	\N	882	929
