3382	The Apostle's Creed didn't appear all at once but rather is slowly developed over time during the first few centuries of the Christian Church. During the early years of Christianity, short summaries were used called the rules of faith. What these statements did was help protect the truth of the gospel, train leaders and also gave ordinary believers a clear way to understand their faith. You have to consider back then most people could not read and the Bible was not widely available so these summaries were very helpful to them. Over time these turned into creeds. These were short easy to remember statements of beliefs. Creeds were often recited during worship services and baptisms so new believers could clearly express their faith. The Old Roman Creed is one of the earliest examples of this. It closely resembled what is known as the Apostle's Creed. At first different churches had slightly different versions of the creed but around A.D. 700, it became standardized into the form we recognize today. This shows us how the early church wanted a unifying statement that could be used everywhere. It also provides a simple way to teach new Christians, help the church stay focused on biblical truth as well as offer protection against false teachings that were common at the time and are still relevant to this day.	0	2025-09-11 07:15:25+05:30	2025-09-11 07:15:25+05:30	\N	912	866
3383	The church believed it was important to create and use a creed for many reasons. One of the first reasons was it gave Christians a clear summery of what they believed. During the early centuries, most people were not educated to read and write and very few people had access to the Bible. These short simple statements like the Apostles' Creed made it possible for everyone to learn the essentials of the Christian faith particularly for new believers as well as those with little to no education. Secondly the creed was also important because of the commonality of false teachings during that time which in fact is still relevant to this day. Groups such as the Gnostics taught that the physical world was evil and denied that Jesus had truly come in the flesh. There were also others like the Docetists that claimed that Jesus only appeared to suffer and die but was not really human. By teaching the creed, churches during that time were able to give Christians a way to guard themselves against these false teachings. Thirdly the creed also played a major role in baptism and discipleship. Whenever new believers were baptized they were asked to confess their faith. The creed played a role here and gave them the words to express their faith in the Father, Son, and Holy Spirit as well their belief in forgiveness, resurrection, and eternal life. This was a confession and proof that they understood at least the basics of the Gospel. Lastly the creed promoted unity among the churches. Christians from different places as well as from different times may have worshiped in different ways. However by sharing the same confession they show that they belonged to the same family of faith in Jesus worldwide.	0	2025-09-11 07:29:27+05:30	2025-09-11 07:29:27+05:30	\N	912	867
3384	The Apostles' Creed teaches that God is the Trinity. This means that there is one God in three persons who are the Father, the Son, and the Holy Spirit. To make more sense of this you need to understand the persons and nature. A person is a distinct self aware individual. The Father, Son, and Spirit are not the same person but rather they are related to each other and do different things. Nature means God's essence or being. All three persons share the same divine nature. What this means is that Christians believe in one God not three separate gods. Going into more detail, the creed shows the different works of each person. The Father for example is almighty and the maker of heaven and earth. His role is creation and ruling over everything. The Son, who is Jesus, was conceived by the Holy Spirit born of the Virgin Mary. Jesus suffered under Pontius Pilate, then died and buried and then rose again on the third day. He is ascended to heave and rules at the right hand of the Father. Jesus will return to judge the world. His name work is salvation which was achieved through His death and resurrection. Lastly the Holy Spirit gives life and works in the church. The creed mentions Him in connection with the Holy Catholic Church, the forgiveness of sins, and life everlasting. The main role here includes creating faith, uniting believers, and applying Christ's salvation to us. In short the Trinity means one God, three persons who is working together in creation, salvation, and in the church.	0	2025-09-11 07:43:27+05:30	2025-09-11 07:43:27+05:30	\N	912	868
3385	It is important to participate in the church because Christianity was not ment to be practiced alone. You can see this from the start that believers came together to worship, learn, and care for one another. The Bible also warns us not to give up meeting together. This is because being with other Christians helps us grow in faith and stay strong. An example of this could be were a person might hear a sermon that helps them understand God's Word more clearly or they may be encouraged when others pray for them during a hard time. Just like a basketball team or a football team needs every player, the church needs every member to use their gifts to serve and build up the whole body. The Apostles's Creed says that we believe in the Holy Catholic Church and the communion of saints. This should tell us that the church is much bigger than one congregation. Rather, it is all believers everywhere and throughout the history of the world. Whenever we gather with the church, we are going something much larger than ourselves. It is also equally important to preserve the church's central doctrines. From the earliest centuries there have been many false teachers who have tried to distort the Gospel by denying truth such as the humanity of Christ, His resurrection, or the forgiveness of sins. This happens even today. Surprisingly even at Calvary Assembly were members of the Shincheonju Church of Jesus came. Reciting and teaching the Apostles' Creed helped the church protect these essential beliefs. Without guarding these truths the church in general could easily drift into false teachings and loose the truth of the Christian message. Participation and preservation ensures that the church remains a faithful community of believers. Gathering in worship and guarding core doctrines is the only way the church can continue its mission to proclaim the Gospel and pass it on for future generations.	0	2025-09-11 08:00:39+05:30	2025-09-11 08:00:39+05:30	\N	912	869
3386	The Apostles' Creed is foundational to Christian theology because it summarizes the most basic and essential truths of the Christian faith. For example, just as you need a solid foundation for a building to stand, Christian beliefs also need a solid starting point. The Creed gives the bases that is needed by setting out who is God, what Christ as done for us, the work of the Holy Spirit, the importance of the church, and the hope of forgiveness, resurrection, and eternal life. One of these ways that the Creed is foundational is that it acts as a standard for testing all other beliefs. If someone claims that Jesus was only a good teacher but not truly God for example, the Creed reminds us of the truth which is Jesus Christ is God's only Son, our Lord. In the same way if a teaching denies the resurrection, the Creeds protects us by affirming the resurrection of the body. This will help keep the true followers of Christ from being misled by convincing false ideas. The Creed is also foundational because it provides the logical basis for other Christian teachings. For example, if God is the maker of heaven and earth then he also has authority over creation and we can trust His power in our lives. If Christ rose from the dead then we can be confident that He too will raise us as well. These are some of the the basic truths which support everything Christians believe. The Apostles' Creed is foundational because it sets boundaries of authentic Christianity which anchors us to Scripture and also provides the core truths on which all other theology is built.	0	2025-09-11 08:12:42+05:30	2025-09-11 08:12:42+05:30	\N	912	870
3387	Christians says that the God of the Bible is the one and true God because evidence of this is found all throughout the scriptures. The Bible repeatedly teaches that there are no other gods. Many other religions call their deities gods but Christians believe that these are imaginary beings or idols that were made up. In some cases they could also be evil beings or spiritual forces. The Bible explains that from the beginning of creation you can see where God has made evidence showing his existence clear for all the world to see. You too can see this evidence of His power and divine nature in creation itself. The sad fact of the matter is that humans have fallen into sin and because of this they refuse to honor God and choose to instead worship false gods or other created beings. The belief that Christians have is the belief in one God which is called monotheism. Similar to and extent to Judaism and Islam which also believe in monotheism. However, there is something different with Christianity that both Judaism and Islam rejects. Christians believe that this one God exists in three persons which are the Father, the Son, and the Holy Spirit. These three persons are not separate gods but share the same divine essence. This God is what Christians believe to have the power to create everything from nothing. Also having the power to ultimately rule over all and save people from their sin. This is clear in the Apostles' Creed when it states that "I believe in God the Father Almighty, Maker of heaven and earth."	10	2025-09-18 06:50:06+05:30	2025-09-18 06:50:06+05:30	\N	913	871
3388	When you use the term simplicity it is easy to fall into the narrative of sounding like it means easy to understand. The truth of the matter is that that is not the case at all. Instead it describes God's essence which is completely unified and not made up of different parts. God is not a mixture of pieces that you put together like love, power, and justice but rather he is one perfect and complete being. All of His qualities are fully present in everything that He does. An example of this that was explained to us to help us understand is the example of a glass of pure water. Pure water is completely water and nothing else. You can by all means add dirt and then it becomes mud. This is then a mixture of two different substances. However, God's essence is not like this at all, His essence is like the pure water which is entirely one and undivided. This is very important to understand especially when Christians believe in one God even though God the Father, Son and Holy Spirit exists. The three persons are not separate gods joined together but rather they share the same exact divine essence. This is what it means to Christians believing in one God while also affirming the Trinity. God's simplicity means that He is unchanging and perfectly consistent. All his attributes work together in perfect harmony. For us believers this means that God can always be trusted. He will always act according to His good and perfect nature.	9	2025-09-18 07:03:58+05:30	2025-09-18 07:03:58+05:30	\N	913	872
3389	Both of these terms, "ontological Trinity" and "economic Trinity" are used in a way for Christians to describe the relationship between God the Father, God the Son, and God the Holy Spirit. The ontological Trinity primarily focuses on who God is in His being. The word ontological means related to being. This term focuses on God's essence showing that all three persons of the Father, the Son, and the Holy Spirit, share the same divine nature. Each person is fully God as well as equal in all power and glory as well as all divine attributes. This helps us remember that there has never been a time when one person has existed without the other. The economic Trinity on the other hand focuses on what God does. In other words, it helps us understand how the three persons relate to each other. This view describes the roles each person has. An example of this is seen when the Father sends the Son into the world. The Son obeys the Father and accomplishes salvation. When then the Holy Spirit applies that salvation to believers. The Father has authority over the Son and the Spirit but is not because He is more powerful or more God like than they are. It is because of their roles to one another. These two views are similar because they both describe the same God and affirm that the Father, Son and Spirit are one. However both are different in respects to the ontological Trinity explains God's being while the economic Trinity explains his actions and relationships.	0	2025-09-18 07:16:31+05:30	2025-09-18 07:16:31+05:30	\N	913	873
